window.SHIJING_EN = {"gf-001": ["Ospreys cry guan-guan, resting on the sandbar in the river.", "A graceful, virtuous maiden is the fine match for a gentleman.", "Uneven water plants drift left and right in the stream.", "That graceful, virtuous maiden—he longs for her day and night.", "He seeks her but cannot win her; waking and sleeping he thinks of her.", "Longing on and on, he tosses and turns, unable to sleep.", "Uneven water plants—we pick them left and right.", "That graceful, virtuous maiden—with zither and harp he draws near to her.", "Uneven water plants—we sort them left and right.", "That graceful, virtuous maiden—with bells and drums he delights her."], "gf-002": ["Kudzu vines spread and fill the valley; the leaves are lush and green.", "Yellow birds fly to and fro, perching on the shrubs, their calls harmonious.", "Kudzu vines spread and fill the valley; the leaves grow dense and layered.", "We cut and boil them, weave fine and coarse cloth, and wear it without tiring of it.", "I tell my governess I am going home to visit my parents.", "I wash my undergarments and rinse my outer clothes.", "I sort what needs washing from what does not, ready to go home and see my parents."], "gf-003": ["I pick and pick the mouse-ear, yet cannot fill even a shallow basket.", "My heart longs for that person; I set the basket down by the roadside.", "I climb that steep rocky height; my horse's legs go soft and weak.", "Let me fill that golden cup, so I stop thinking of him all the time.", "I climb that high ridge; my horse grows dizzy and spent.", "Let me fill that horn cup, so I do not grieve too deeply.", "I climb that boulder-strewn hill; the horse is sick, the servant worn out—how can I not sigh in sorrow?"], "gf-004": ["In the south stands a bent tree; kudzu vines twine up around it.", "Happy gentleman—blessings and prosperity comfort him.", "In the south stands a bent tree; kudzu vines cover it over.", "Happy gentleman—blessings and prosperity shield him.", "In the south stands a bent tree; kudzu vines coil about it.", "Happy gentleman—blessings and prosperity have made him complete."], "gf-005": ["Locusts beat their wings, swarming in dense throngs.", "May your children and grandchildren be many and flourish with promise.", "Locusts beat their wings, humming as they go.", "May your descendants stretch on, generation after generation.", "Locusts beat their wings, gathering together.", "May your children live in harmony, settled and thriving."], "gf-006": ["The peach tree is young and tender; its blossoms blaze a vivid red.", "This maiden is married now; she will make the household harmonious.", "The peach tree is young and tender; its fruit hangs full and ripe.", "This maiden is married now; she will bring peace to the family rooms.", "The peach tree is young and tender; its leaves grow thick and green.", "This maiden is married now; she will make the household get along."], "gf-007": ["Rabbit nets are tightly spread; wooden stakes are driven with a ding-ding.", "A mighty warrior—he is the shield of lords and princes.", "Rabbit nets are tightly spread, set at the great crossroads.", "A mighty warrior—he is a fine helper to lords and princes.", "Rabbit nets are tightly spread, set among the woods.", "A mighty warrior—he is the trusted confidant of lords and princes."], "gf-008": ["We pick plantain, pick plantain—let us go gather it.", "We pick plantain, pick plantain—we have gathered some already.", "We pick plantain, pick plantain—picking the seeds one by one.", "We pick plantain, pick plantain—stripping them handful by handful.", "We pick plantain, pick plantain—lifting our skirts to hold them.", "We pick plantain, pick plantain—tucking our skirts full of them."], "gf-009": ["In the south there are tall trees, yet one cannot rest beneath them.", "On the Han River there are roaming girls, yet one cannot pursue them.", "The Han is too wide—one cannot swim across.", "The river is too long—even a raft cannot ferry over.", "Tangled brushwood sticks up; go cut those thorn branches.", "If that maiden should marry, I would gladly feed her horses well.", "The Han is too wide—one cannot swim across.", "The river is too long—even a raft cannot ferry over.", "Tangled brushwood sticks up; go cut those mugwort stems.", "If that maiden should marry, I would gladly feed her little horses well.", "The Han is too wide—one cannot swim across.", "The river is too long—even a raft cannot ferry over."], "gf-010": ["Along the embankment of the Ru I cut branches and trunks.", "Not seeing my beloved, I hunger like one fasting at dawn.", "Along the embankment of the Ru I cut the fresh young shoots.", "I have seen my beloved—he has not grown distant from me.", "The bream's tail has turned red from strain; the royal house is in peril as if on fire.", "Though the danger is like fire, my parents are still close at hand."], "gf-011": ["The unicorn's hooves—the young lords are kind and capable; O unicorn!", "The unicorn's brow—the noble clansmen are kind and capable; O unicorn!", "The unicorn's horns—the kinsmen are kind and capable; O unicorn!"], "gf-012": ["The magpie has built its nest; the dove moves in to dwell.", "This maiden is marrying; a hundred carriages come to receive her.", "The magpie has built its nest; the dove takes possession of it.", "This maiden is marrying; a hundred carriages come to escort her.", "The magpie has built its nest; doves crowd it full.", "This maiden is marrying; a hundred carriages come to complete the rites."], "gf-013": ["Where shall we gather white southernwood?", "On the islets in the ponds.", "What will we use it for?", "For the lords' ancestral sacrifices.", "Where shall we gather white southernwood?", "In the mountain streams.", "What will we use it for?", "For the lords' ancestral temples.", "With hairpieces piled high, we bustle morning and evening on official business.", "With hairpieces splendid and many, when the work is done we go home."], "gf-014": ["Grass insects chirp; grasshoppers hop and leap.", "Not seeing my beloved, my heart is heavy with worry.", "Now that I have seen him, now that we have met, my heart can settle.", "I climb the southern mountain to gather ferns.", "Not seeing my beloved, my heart is restless with care.", "Now that I have seen him, now that we have met, my heart is glad.", "I climb the southern mountain to gather wild peas.", "Not seeing my beloved, my heart is filled with sorrow.", "Now that I have seen him, now that we have met, my heart grows calm."], "gf-015": ["Where shall we gather duckweed?", "By the southern mountain stream.", "Where shall we gather waterweed?", "In those running shallows.", "What shall we hold it in?", "Square baskets and round hampers.", "What shall we cook it in?", "Tripod pots and cauldrons.", "Where shall we make the offering?", "Beneath the ancestral temple window.", "Who will preside at the rite?", "That reverent young maiden."], "gf-016": ["The sweet pear tree's shade is dense—do not prune, do not cut; Lord Shao once lodged here.", "The sweet pear tree's shade is dense—do not prune, do not spoil; Lord Shao once rested here.", "The sweet pear tree's shade is dense—do not prune, do not break; Lord Shao once stopped here."], "gf-017": ["The road is wet with dew; it is not that I dislike traveling by night—I only fear the dew is too heavy.", "Who says the sparrow has no horns?", "How else could it peck through my roof?", "Who says you have no household?", "How else do you drag me before the court?", "Even if you drag me to court, you still lack what it takes for marriage!", "Who says the rat has no teeth?", "How else could it gnaw through my wall?", "Who says you have no household?", "How else do you force me into a lawsuit?", "Even if you force me to sue, I will never yield to you!"], "gf-018": ["A lambskin robe, stitched with white silk in five seams.", "Business done, he goes home to eat, walking with an easy, leisurely gait.", "A lambskin coat, stitched with white silk in five joins.", "With an easy, leisurely gait he comes from the office home to eat.", "A lambskin garment, stitched with white silk in five bindings.", "With an easy, leisurely gait, business done, he goes home to eat."], "gf-019": ["Thunder rolls and rolls on the sunny side of the southern mountain.", "Why leave this place and dare not take a little ease?", "Loyal, kind gentleman—come home, come home!", "Thunder rolls and rolls beside the southern mountain.", "Why leave this place and dare not rest a little?", "Loyal, kind gentleman—come home, come home!", "Thunder rolls and rolls at the foot of the southern mountain.", "Why leave this place and dare not settle even briefly?", "Loyal, kind gentleman—come home, come home!"], "gf-020": ["The plums are falling; seven-tenths still remain on the tree.", "Young men who seek me—come on this auspicious day.", "The plums are falling; only three-tenths remain on the tree.", "Young men who seek me—come this very day.", "The plums are falling; gather them in a shallow basket.", "Young men who seek me—just speak up and say the word."], "xy-001": ["The deer cry you-you, eating mugwort in the wilds.", "I have honored guests; we play the se and blow the sheng.", "Blowing the sheng and sounding its reeds for cheer, we present baskets full of gifts.", "People treat me with true kindness and show me the right path.", "The deer cry you-you, eating green artemisia in the wilds.", "I have honored guests; their fair reputation shines brightly.", "They treat the people without frivolity—gentlemen should model themselves on this and learn.", "I have fine wine; let the guests feast and roam at ease.", "The deer cry you-you, eating qin grass in the wilds.", "I have honored guests; we play the se and the qin.", "Playing se and qin, we are harmonious, joyful, and thoroughly pleased.", "I have fine wine to delight my guests' hearts."], "xy-002": ["Four stallions pull the carriage without rest; the great road winds long and far.", "Do I not long to go home?", "The king's business never ends, and my heart is sad.", "Four stallions pull the carriage without rest; the white horses pant with exhaustion.", "Do I not long to go home?", "The king's business never ends; there is no time to settle and rest.", "The turtledoves flutter, now high, now low, and settle among the oak thickets.", "The king's business never ends; there is no time to care for my father.", "The turtledoves flutter, flying and pausing, and settle among the wolfberry thickets.", "The king's business never ends; there is no time to care for my mother.", "Driving four white horses, we race urgently along the road.", "Do I not long to go home?", "So I make this song, to sing out my longing for my mother."], "xy-003": ["The flowers bloom in brilliant glory, covering the highlands and the lowlands.", "The envoy hurries along the road, often fearing the mission will not be done in time.", "My horses are young colts; the six reins are smooth as oil.", "We gallop and drive, inquiring and consulting everywhere.", "My horses are blue-black; the six reins are fine as silk.", "We gallop and drive, seeking counsel and plans everywhere.", "My horses are white with black manes; the six reins gleam finely.", "We gallop and drive, deliberating and weighing matters everywhere.", "My horses are dappled gray; the six reins are evenly matched.", "We gallop and drive, asking and seeking advice everywhere."], "xy-004": ["The cherry blossoms open; their calyxes are bright and fair.", "Among people in the world today, none compare to brothers.", "When the threat of death and mourning comes, brothers care most.", "Gathering on highlands and lowlands, brothers seek one another out.", "Wagtails settle on the plain; brothers rush to help in crisis.", "Even with good friends, one can only sigh in vain.", "Though brothers quarrel within the walls, they unite against outside insult.", "Even with good friends, lasting help is hard to find.", "When mourning and turmoil have settled, there is peace and quiet.", "Though one has brothers, are they really no better than friends?", "Set out the bian and dou vessels; drink the fine wine to your heart's content.", "When all the brothers are gathered, there is harmony and warmth.", "Affection with wife and children is like playing the se and the qin.", "When brothers are in accord, there is harmony and deep delight.", "Make your household secure; make your wife and children happy.", "Think it over carefully—is this not truly so?"], "xy-005": ["The sound of chopping wood rings ding-ding; the birds call ying-ying.", "They fly from the deep valley and move to the high trees.", "Calling ying-ying, they seek an answering friend.", "Look at those birds—even they seek a friend's reply.", "How much more for people—how can one not seek friends?", "If the spirits hear this, there will at last be harmony and peace.", "Chopping wood sounds xu-xu; clear filtered wine is fragrant.", "We already have a plump tender lamb; please invite the elder uncles.", "Better that they happen not to come than that I be blamed for neglect.", "The courtyard is swept spotless; eight gui of fine dishes are set out.", "We already have a fat ram; please invite the maternal uncles.", "Better that they happen not to come than that I be blamed for discourtesy.", "Chopping wood on the hillside; the filtered wine overflows.", "The bian and dou are set in neat rows; brothers, do not grow distant.", "If a person loses kindness, even a small matter of dry rations can breed resentment.", "If there is wine, strain it for me to drink; if there is none, go buy some for me.", "Drumbeats boom for me; dancers squat and leap for me.", "When I have leisure again, come drink this clear wine."], "xy-006": ["Heaven keeps you secure; your foundation is utterly firm.", "It makes your blessings rich and full—what blessing does it not grant you?", "It makes you gain in abundance; nothing fails to flourish in plenty.", "Heaven keeps you secure and lets you receive fortune and salary.", "In all things nothing is unfit; you receive Heaven's countless emoluments.", "It grants you lasting blessings—only fearing there are not days enough to use them.", "Heaven keeps you secure; in all things nothing fails to prosper.", "Like mountains and hills, like ridges and mounds, like rivers rolling in—nothing fails to grow day by day.", "Prepare the sacrificial food in purity, to offer with filial reverence.", "In spring, summer, autumn, and winter, offer sacrifice to the former dukes and kings.", "The impersonator of the dead conveys the words: May you have boundless longevity.", "The spirits have descended and leave you many blessings.", "The common people are simple and honest, seeking only their daily food and drink.", "The multitudes of the people all receive the transforming influence of your virtue.", "Like the moon always full, like the sun rising in the east.", "Long-lived as the southern mountains, neither deficient nor collapsing.", "Flourishing like pine and cypress, nothing fails to continue and multiply."], "xy-007": ["Gathering wei greens, gathering wei greens—the sprouts have just come up.", "Talk of going home, talk of going home—another year is nearly at its end.", "No time for home and family, only because the Xianyun are invading.", "No time to settle and rest, only because the Xianyun are invading.", "Gathering wei greens, gathering wei greens—the leaves are soft and tender.", "Talk of going home, talk of going home—my heart grows more anxious.", "Anxiety burns like fire; I am hungry and thirsty.", "Garrison posts have no fixed place; no one carries word home for me.", "Gathering wei greens, gathering wei greens—the stems have grown hard.", "Talk of going home, talk of going home—it is the tenth month, the sunny month, again.", "The king's business never ends; there is no time to rest.", "My heart aches with worry—I fear this campaign will not bring me back!", "What is that blooming so richly?", "It is the cherry blossom.", "What is that great carriage?", "It is the commander's war chariot.", "The war chariot is harnessed; four stallions stand tall and strong.", "How dare we settle in one place?", "In a single month we report victory many times.", "Driving those four stallions, the horses are strong and vigorous.", "The commander relies on them; the soldiers take cover behind them.", "The four horses stand in neat ranks, with ivory bow-tips and fish-skin quivers.", "How can we not be on guard every day?", "The Xianyun press too urgently!", "When I left long ago, the willows swayed gently.", "Now as I return, rain and snow fall thick and fast.", "The road goes slowly; I am thirsty and hungry.", "My heart is sorrowful—who knows my grief!"], "xy-008": ["I send out the war chariots, to that pasture ground.", "From the Son of Heaven I was summoned here.", "I gather the chariot drivers and tell them to load and set out.", "The king's business is full of peril; the situation is urgent.", "I send out the war chariots, to the outskirts.", "Raise the turtle-and-snake banners, and set up the yak-tail standards.", "Those bird-of-prey flags and turtle-and-snake banners—how can they not flutter and snap?", "Anxiety weighs quietly; the chariot drivers look haggard too.", "The king commands Nanzhong to go north and build walls.", "War chariots rumble; banners are bright and clear.", "The Son of Heaven orders me to build walls in Shuofang.", "Illustrious Nanzhong sweeps away the Xianyun.", "When I left long ago, the millet was in flower.", "Now as I return, rain and snow fill the road.", "The king's business is full of peril; there is no time to settle.", "Do I not long to go home?", "I only fear these urgent military orders.", "Grass insects chirp yao-yao; grasshoppers hop and leap.", "Before I see my gentleman, my heart is full of worry.", "Once I see my gentleman, my heart is at ease.", "Illustrious Nanzhong campaigns against the western Rong.", "Spring days stretch long and slow; plants grow lush and green.", "Orioles call jie-jie; gatherers of white aster are many and busy.", "Captives taken, enemy crowds led along—now we are about to return.", "Illustrious Nanzhong—the Xianyun are already pacified."], "xy-009": ["That solitary wild pear tree—its fruit is round and bright.", "The king's business never ends; day after day it drags on.", "It is already the tenth month, the sunny month; the woman's heart aches—the campaigner should have leave by now.", "That solitary wild pear tree—its leaves grow lush and thick.", "The king's business never ends; my heart is sad.", "Plants grow lush and green; the woman's heart is bitter—the campaigner should be coming home!", "Climbing that northern mountain to gather wolfberries.", "The king's business never ends, making my parents worry for me.", "The sandalwood cart moves slowly; the four horses are worn out—the campaigner should not be far.", "No cart comes, no one returns; anxiety cuts to the bone.", "The appointed time has passed and still he does not arrive, adding still more worry.", "Divination by tortoise and milfoil both say he is nearly here—the campaigner is already close."], "xy-010": ["Fish fall into the creel—there are yellow-cheeked fish and sharks.", "The gentleman has wine, fine and plentiful.", "Fish fall into the creel—there are bream and snakehead.", "The gentleman has wine, plentiful and fine.", "Fish fall into the creel—there are catfish and carp.", "The gentleman has wine, fine and abundant.", "How many the products are, and how good they are!", "How fine the products are, and how complete they are!", "How abundant the products are, and how timely they are!"], "dy-001": ["King Wen's spirit is above; his radiance shines clear in Heaven.", "Zhou may be an ancient state, yet Heaven's mandate has made it new.", "Is Zhou not illustrious? Is the Lord's command not timely?", "King Wen ascends and descends, always at the side of the Lord on High.", "Indefatigable King Wen—his fair renown never ceases.", "Rich grace was bestowed on Zhou, and reached King Wen's descendants.", "King Wen's line stretches through a hundred generations; the gentlemen of Zhou also shine age after age.", "Those whose houses are not yet famous still act with careful reverence.", "How many outstanding men were born in this kingdom.", "That the kingdom can raise talent—these are Zhou's pillars; with so many able men, King Wen rests in peace.", "Solemn King Wen—bright, and reverent.", "How great is Heaven's mandate, fallen upon Shang's descendants.", "Shang's descendants—numbering more than a hundred million.", "Once the Lord on High had given the command, they submitted to Zhou.", "Submitting to Zhou shows that Heaven's mandate does not stay with one house forever.", "The able and keen gentlemen of Yin come to the capital to assist at the libation rite.", "When they pour the libation they still wear Yin's embroidered robes and Yin caps.", "Loyal ministers of the king—do you not think of your ancestors?", "To think of your ancestors, you must cultivate your own virtue.", "Forever match Heaven's mandate, and seek abundant blessing for yourselves.", "Before Yin lost the people's hearts, it too could match the Lord on High.", "Take Yin as a mirror: the great mandate is not easily kept!", "Heaven's mandate is hard to hold—do not let it fail through your own person.", "Proclaim a fair and righteous name, and remember that Yin's rise and fall came from Heaven.", "Heaven acts without sound, without scent.", "Model yourselves on King Wen, and the myriad states will trust you."], "dy-002": ["On earth clarity is plain to see; in Heaven majesty blazes bright.", "Heaven's will is hard to fathom yet sure; to be king is never easy.", "The throne once belonged to Yin's rightful heir, yet Heaven would not let him rule the four quarters.", "A daughter of the Ren clan of Zhi came from Shang, married into Zhou, and became a lady of the capital.", "She was matched with King Ji, and devoted herself to virtue and right.", "Great Ren conceived and bore this King Wen.", "This very King Wen was careful and wary.", "Brightly he served the Lord on High, and drew down many blessings.", "His conduct was never crooked, and so he received the allegiance of every state.", "Heaven looked down upon the earth; the mandate had already gathered.", "In King Wen's early years Heaven made a match for him.", "North of the Xia River, by the banks of the Wei.", "King Wen praised this marriage: a great state had a fine daughter.", "That daughter of a great state was beautiful as a sister of Heaven.", "Betrothal gifts fixed the auspicious day; he went in person to welcome her at the Wei.", "Boats were joined into a bridge—how splendid was the wedding.", "The mandate came down from Heaven and ordained this King Wen.", "In Zhou, in the capital, he took again a bride—a daughter of Shen.", "The eldest son walked the right path, and with sincerity was born King Wu.", "Heaven protected and commanded you: unite and strike great Shang.", "Shang's armies gathered thick as a forest.", "They arrayed at Muye; only our Zhou lord rose in force.", "The Lord on High is watching you—do not be of two minds.", "Muye was broad; sandalwood chariots shone; four strong horses thundered on.", "Grand Preceptor Shangfu soared like an eagle.", "He aided King Wu in a great strike on Shang; in one morning the world grew clear."], "dy-003": ["Melons and gourds trail on without end.", "When the Zhou people first rose, it was from the Du to the Qi streams.", "Ancient Duke Danfu dug kiln-caves to dwell in; there were not yet houses and halls.", "Ancient Duke Danfu set out at dawn, driving his horses.", "Along the western water's edge he came beneath Mount Qi.", "With his Jiang consort he came to survey a place to live.", "The Zhou plain was rich and fair; even bitter greens tasted sweet as syrup.", "So they began to plan; they scorched the tortoise and asked the omen—fit to dwell, fit in season—and built their halls here.", "Then they settled in: divided left and right, fixed borders and fields, cut ditches and raised ridges.", "From west to east, everywhere people were at work.", "They summoned the Minister of Works and the Minister of Education to raise the dwellings.", "Plumb-lines were stretched straight; frames held the walls; the ancestral temple stood solemn and ordered.", "Earth was loaded with a rumble, flung with a roar, pounded with a thud, pared with a scrape.", "A hundred walls rose together; even the great drums could not drown the sound of labor.", "Then they raised the Gao Gate—and the Gao Gate was tall.", "Then they raised the Ying Gate—and the Ying Gate was strict and fine.", "Then they built the great altar of the soil; from there the war host set out.", "Though anger was not wholly spent, his fair name was not diminished.", "Oak and thorn were cleared away; the roads ran open.", "The Hunyi fled, gasping without pause!", "Yu and Rui came seeking judgment; King Wen moved their hearts toward goodness.", "I say there are devoted adherents; I say there are aides before and behind.", "I say there are those who run to serve; I say there are those who ward off foreign insult!"], "dy-004": ["Yupu trees grow lush and thick; we cut them and pile them for fuel.", "The solemn king—those at his left and right hurry to follow.", "The solemn king—those at his left and right hold jade zhang tablets.", "Bearing the zhang, their bearing is grave; fine gentlemen suit the rite.", "On the Jing River boats race; the crew pulls oars as one.", "The Zhou king marches out; the six armies follow.", "The vast River of Heaven spreads its pattern across the sky.", "May the Zhou king live long—how could he not nurture talent?", "Carved into patterned grace, his substance is like gold and jade.", "Our diligent king sets the order for the four quarters."], "dy-005": ["Look to the foot of Mount Han: hazel and hu thick and dense.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman seeks blessing also by ease and cheer.", "The jade ladle shines; yellow wine flows within.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—blessings and prosperity descend.", "Kites soar into high Heaven; fish leap into the deep pool.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—how could he not nurture talent?", "Clear wine is already poured; the red bull is already prepared.", "They are used for the offering, to pray for great blessing.", "Oak and thorn stand dense—fuel for the people's fire-sacrifice.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—the spirits give him comfort and reward.", "Kudzu vines sprawl and climb the branches.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman seeks blessing without taking crooked paths."], "dy-006": ["Dignified Great Ren, mother of King Wen; fair Zhou Jiang, lady of the royal house.", "Great Si inherited virtue and renown, and so bore many sons.", "She showed kindness to the former dukes; the spirits had no grievance, no pain.", "First she set the example among the principal wives, then extended it to brothers, and so ordered house and state.", "In the palace there was harmony; in the temple, reverence.", "Though not showy, it was as if a spirit were present; though never weary, she could still keep herself secure.", "Thus great calamities did not exhaust them, and disease did not strike.", "What she had not heard of still fitted the rule; what was not yet remonstrated she could still accept.", "Thus adults had virtue, and the young had achievement.", "The ancients never wearied of selecting these fine gentlemen."], "dy-007": ["How great is the Lord on High, looking down in blazing majesty.", "He surveys the four quarters, seeking peace for the people.", "These two states—their rule had lost the people's hearts.", "So among the states of the four quarters he searched and measured.", "The Lord on High loathed them, hated their spreading borders.", "Then he turned his favor to the west, and made it a place of settled dwelling.", "He had cut away and cast aside the dead and overshadowing trees.", "He had leveled and cleared the thickets of scrub.", "He opened and cleared the tamarisk and ju trees.", "He rooted out and cleaned away the mountain mulberry and zhe.", "The Lord moved a man of bright virtue; the Chuanyi fled defeated on the road.", "Heaven set a matching lord; the receipt of the mandate was already firm.", "The Lord surveyed the ridges: oak and thorn cleared, pine and cypress standing straight.", "The Lord founded a matching state, beginning with Taibo and King Ji.", "This King Ji was friendly by nature.", "Loving his elder brother, he thickened blessing and joy, and was given glory.", "The emoluments he received were not lost; he possessed the four quarters throughout.", "This King Ji—the Lord weighed his heart.", "He quieted his virtuous reputation; his virtue could shine.", "Able to shine, able to treat his kind well; able to lead, able to be a lord.", "King of this great state, able to yield, able to draw others near.", "As for King Wen, his virtue left nothing to regret.", "Having received the Lord's blessing, it extended to his descendants.", "The Lord said to King Wen: Do not be overbearing or violent; do not covet; first climb the high bank.", "The Mi people were not compliant; they dared resist the great state, invading Ruan toward Gong.", "The king flared in anger, ordered his troops, and checked the invading host.", "Thus he thickened Zhou's blessing, and answered the world.", "He camped by the capital grounds and advanced from Ruan's border.", "Climb my high ridge—do not array troops on my hills and tombs.", "My tombs, my slopes—do not drink from my springs, my springs and pools.", "He surveyed that fair plain, dwelling south of Mount Qi, beside the Wei.", "A model for the myriad states, a lord for the people below.", "The Lord said to King Wen: I favor bright virtue—not by loud severity, not by rod and threat.", "Not knowing, not noticing—only following the Lord's rule.", "The Lord said to King Wen: Consult your friendly states; assemble your brothers.", "With your grappling hooks, with your siege towers and battering rams, assault the walls of Chong.", "Siege towers and rams advanced at ease; Chong's walls stood high.", "Captives were taken in strings; left ears were cut off in calm order.", "Sacrifices to Heaven and to the horse-spirit brought submission; the four quarters dared not insult them.", "Siege towers and rams grew strong; Chong's walls were steep.", "Then came the assault and the strike; then came cutting off and wiping out.", "Thus the four quarters dared not defy."], "dy-008": ["They began to build the Spirit Terrace, planning and managing.", "The people came to build it; in no many days it was done.", "The work was not pressed; the people came like children to a father.", "The king was in the Spirit Park; the does lay at rest.", "The does were sleek and glossy; the white birds clean and bright.", "The king was at the Spirit Pool; the whole pond leapt with fish.", "The bell-frame had carved teeth; there were great drums and great bells.", "They struck drum and bell in rhythm; joy was in the Circular College.", "They struck drum and bell in rhythm; joy was in the Circular College.", "The alligator-skin drums boomed.", "Blind musicians struck up the music of great achievement."], "dy-009": ["The heirs with martial merit are Zhou's; generation after generation there are wise kings.", "The three former lords are in Heaven; the present king is matched with them in the capital.", "The king is matched in the capital, that virtue may continue age after age.", "Forever match Heaven's mandate, and perfect the king's good faith.", "The king's good faith is the model for all under Heaven.", "Forever cherish filial thought—filial thought is the rule.", "Love and honor this one man, and the feudal lords all follow his virtue.", "Forever cherish filial thought—how bright the inheritance of the great work.", "Brightly guide those who come after, following the ancestors' footprints.", "On to ten thousand years, receiving Heaven's blessing.", "Receiving Heaven's blessing, the four quarters come to congratulate.", "On to ten thousand years—how could there be no helpers?"], "dy-010": ["King Wen had renown—indeed great renown.", "He sought peace, and at last saw success.", "How great was King Wen!", "King Wen received the mandate and had this martial achievement.", "After conquering Chong, he built a settlement at Feng.", "How great was King Wen!", "They built walls and dug moats, making Feng to match the work.", "Not rushing after private desire, but recalling and fulfilling filial duty.", "How great was the royal lady!", "The king's achievement shone clear—it was the walls of Feng.", "The four quarters assembled; the royal lady was a pillar.", "How great was the royal lady!", "The Feng River flows east—that is the merit of Great Yu.", "The four quarters assembled; the august king was their lord.", "How great was the august king!", "Haojing had its Circular College; from west and east, south and north, none failed to submit in heart.", "How great was the august king!", "They divined and asked the king about settling at Haojing.", "The tortoise confirmed it; King Wu completed the matter.", "How great was King Wu!", "By the Feng there is qi grass—would King Wu not undertake great works?", "He left plans for his descendants, to settle and support those who come after.", "How great was King Wu!"], "dy-011": ["She who first gave birth to the Zhou people was Jiang Yuan.", "How did she bear the people?", "She could sacrifice with pure sincerity, seeking to cast off the sorrow of childlessness.", "She stepped on the Lord of High's footprint at the big toe and her heart rejoiced; then she rested, then she conceived in reverence.", "Then she bore and reared him—that was Hou Ji.", "When the months were full, the first birth came as smooth as a lamb's.", "No tear, no rupture, no disaster, no harm.", "Thereby his numinous wonder was made plain.", "Was the Lord on High unsettled? Did he not accept the pure sacrifice?—yet a child was born.", "They laid him in a narrow lane; cattle and sheep sheltered and suckled him.", "They laid him in a level wood; just then people were felling trees.", "They laid him on cold ice; birds covered him with their wings.", "When the birds flew off, Hou Ji cried out.", "The cry was long and loud, filling the road.", "When he could crawl, he was already clever and aware.", "He sought food for his own mouth.", "He planted soybeans; the soybeans grew lush and waving.", "Grain ears hung down; hemp and wheat grew dense; melons and gourds clustered thick.", "Hou Ji planted crops by a way that helped them thrive.", "He cleared the thick weeds and sowed the fine grain.", "Seeds sprouted and budded; the shoots grew and rose.", "They jointed and headed; the kernels grew firm and fair.", "Ears hung heavy and full—and so there was the household of Tai.", "Heaven sent down fine seed: black millet and double-grained millet, red millet and white.", "They sowed black and double-grained millet everywhere, reaped and heaped them in the fields.", "They sowed red and white millet everywhere, carried them on shoulders and backs.", "They brought them home and began the sacrifice.", "How do we sacrifice?", "Some pound, some scoop; some winnow, some tread.", "The rinsing of rice sounds shou-shou; steam from the cooking rises floating.", "Then they plan and consider.", "They take mugwort and sacrificial fat, take a ram for the road-spirit, roast and grill, seeking next year's prosperity.", "I heap it in the dou vessels, in dou and in deng.", "The fragrance begins to rise; the Lord on High comes at ease to enjoy it.", "How timely is this fragrance.", "Hou Ji founded the sacrifice.", "May there be no guilt and no regret—handed down even to this day."], "dy-012": ["Reeds grow thick by the roadside; let cattle and sheep not trample them.", "Just budding, just taking form, the leaves soft and moist.", "Close brothers—do not grow distant; all come near.", "Some spread the banquet; some present the armrests.", "Banquet and mats are set; armrests are given with attendants in succession.", "Some offer wine, some return the toast; they wash the jue and set down the jia.", "Meat sauces are served; some roast, some grill.", "Fine dishes include spleen and cheek; some sing, some beat the drum.", "The carved bow is already strong, the four arrows even; shots are fair; guests are ranked by worth.", "The carved bow is drawn full; four arrows are already nocked.", "Four arrows stand like planted trees; ranking guests is done without slight or scorn.", "The great-grandson is host; the wine and sweet brew are rich; with a great ladle he pours, praying for yellow-haired long life.", "Yellow-haired, bent-backed elders lead and support.", "Long life is auspicious, aiding great blessing."], "dy-013": ["Already drunk on wine, already filled with virtue.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; great blessing is granted you.", "Already drunk on wine; your dishes are prepared.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; brightness is granted you.", "Brightness warm and full, a high and clear good end—and a good end that opens anew.", "The impersonator of the dead speaks fair words.", "What does he say?", "The bian and dou vessels are clean and fine.", "Friends assist one another, assisting with dignified bearing.", "The bearing suits the season well; the gentleman has filial sons.", "Filial sons never fail; forever you are granted ones of the same kind.", "What is that same kind?", "Households fair and harmonious throughout.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; forever blessing is granted to his heirs.", "What are those heirs?", "Heaven covers you with rank and emolument.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; the great mandate has its attachments.", "What are those attachments?", "He grants you a virtuous woman.", "He grants you a virtuous woman, and with her sons and grandsons."], "dy-014": ["Wild ducks and gulls are on the Jing; the impersonator comes to feast and be at peace.", "Your wine is already clear; your dishes already fragrant.", "The impersonator feasts; blessings and prosperity come to complete the rite.", "Wild ducks and gulls are on the sandbank; the impersonator comes to feast and find what suits.", "Your wine is already plentiful; your dishes already fine.", "The impersonator feasts; blessings and prosperity come to help.", "Wild ducks and gulls are on the islet; the impersonator comes to feast and settle at ease.", "Your wine is already strained clear; your dishes are dried meat.", "The impersonator feasts; blessings and prosperity descend.", "Wild ducks and gulls are where the streams meet; the impersonator comes to feast and be honored; once he feasts in the ancestral temple, blessings and prosperity arrive.", "The impersonator feasts; blessings and prosperity grow still more lofty.", "Wild ducks and gulls are at the gorge mouth; the impersonator arrives glad and bright.", "Fine wine is glad; roasted meats are fragrant.", "The impersonator feasts; afterward there is no hardship."], "dy-015": ["A fine and cheerful gentleman, illustrious in virtue.", "Fitting for the people, fitting for men; he receives emolument from Heaven.", "Heaven protects and appoints him, declaring it from above.", "Seeking emolument he gains a hundred blessings; sons and grandsons number a thousand million.", "Solemn and august, fit to be lord, fit to be king.", "He errs not, forgets not his roots, and follows the old statutes.", "His bearing is strict; his virtuous words are well ordered.", "Without resentment, without hatred, he follows his ministers and peers.", "Receiving boundless blessing, he is the guiding cord of the four quarters.", "With cord and with thread, peace reaches his friends.", "A hundred feudal lords and ministers love and honor the Son of Heaven.", "In office he does not grow slack—he is where the people rest in peace."], "dy-016": ["Loyal and substantial Duke Liu neither took ease nor idled.", "He fixed field borders and boundaries, stored grain in barns; wrapped dry rations and packed them in bags and sacks.", "Thinking of harmony and glory, bows and arrows were strung; shields, spears, axes and battle-axes were raised—then they set out.", "Loyal and substantial Duke Liu surveyed this plain.", "The people were many and thriving, harmonious and at ease; there was no long sighing.", "He climbed the little hills, then went down to the level land.", "What did he wear at his belt?", "Jade and precious stones, and a knife with a jade-inlaid sheath.", "Loyal and substantial Duke Liu went to those hundred springs.", "He gazed over the broad plain and climbed the southern ridge.", "Then he saw the Jing ground—the capital's open fields.", "Then they settled, then lodged, then talked, then conversed.", "Loyal and substantial Duke Liu took his stand at Jing.", "Their steps were ordered and numerous; he had them set banquet and armrests.", "He mounted his seat and leaned; then he announced the rite to the host of spirits.", "They caught a pig from the sty and poured wine with a gourd ladle.", "They gave him food and drink, and raised him as lord and as clan head.", "Loyal and substantial Duke Liu—the land was both broad and long.", "He measured the sun's shadow from the ridge, studied the yin and yang sides, watched the flowing springs.", "The army took turns in three shifts; he surveyed low wetlands and level plains.", "He ordered the fields and gathered grain, surveying the sunset lands of the western hills.", "The dwellings in Bin were indeed spacious.", "Loyal and substantial Duke Liu built lodgings in Bin.", "They crossed the Wei, took grindstones and forge-stones; the base was then put in order.", "Then people and goods were plenty; they lived along both sides of the Huang Gorge.", "They went upstream along the crossing gorge.", "The settlers grew dense, pressing toward the river's bends."], "dy-017": ["From far off we scoop the standing water by the road, pour it here—enough to steam rice.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman is father and mother to the people.", "From far off we scoop the standing water by the road, pour it here—enough to wash the wine vessels.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman is where the people gather in allegiance.", "From far off we scoop the standing water by the road, pour it here—enough to wash and rinse clean.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman is where the people rest in peace."], "dy-018": ["There is a winding hillside hollow; a whirlwind comes from the south.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman comes to stroll and to sing, setting forth what is in his heart.", "You roam at ease, you wander free; you rest at leisure, you take repose.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—may you live out your full years, ending well like the former dukes.", "Your territory and map are also vast and substantial.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—may you live out your full years; the hundred spirits take you as their host.", "Your receipt of the mandate has been long; blessings and prosperity have made you well.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—may you live out your full years; great blessing always attends you.", "There are supports and wings, filial piety and virtue, to guide and to assist.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—the four quarters take him as their rule.", "His bearing is lofty and fine, like a gui, like a zhang; fair name, fair renown.", "The easy, cheerful gentleman—the four quarters take him as their guiding cord.", "The phoenix is in flight; wingbeats rustle; they also gather and perch.", "The king has many auspicious gentlemen in throngs, at the gentleman's command, loving the Son of Heaven.", "The phoenix is in flight; wingbeats rustle; they also soar and cling to Heaven.", "The king has many auspicious men in throngs, obeying the gentleman's orders, cherishing the common people.", "The phoenix has called—on that high ridge.", "The paulownia has grown—on that sunlit slope.", "Leaves dense and lush; the phoenix calls in harmonious chorus.", "The gentleman's carriages are many and numerous.", "The gentleman's horses are both trained and swift.", "The verses I set forth are not many—only to complete this song."], "dy-019": ["The people are worn with toil; it is about time they found a little ease.", "Show kindness to this central realm, to settle the four quarters.", "Do not indulge the cunning who only comply; beware of the base.", "Check robbery and cruelty—they do not even fear the clear law.", "Win over the distant, be kind to the near, to settle our king.", "The people are worn with toil; it is about time they found a little rest.", "Show kindness to this central realm, that the people may gather as one.", "Do not indulge the cunning who only comply; beware of clamor and confusion.", "Check robbery and cruelty; do not let the people grow anxious.", "Do not cast away your merit; thereby perfect the king's goodness.", "The people are worn with toil; it is about time they caught their breath.", "Show kindness to this capital, to settle the four states.", "Do not indulge the cunning who only comply; beware of conduct without limit.", "Check robbery and cruelty; do not let them do evil.", "Revere your dignified bearing, and draw near to the virtuous.", "The people are worn with toil; it is about time they took a little pause.", "Show kindness to this central realm, that the people's grief may find an outlet.", "Do not indulge the cunning who only comply; beware of ugliness and violence.", "Check robbery and cruelty; do not let the right way be ruined.", "Though you are young, your effect is great.", "The people are worn with toil; it is about time they found a little peace.", "Show kindness to this central realm, that within the state there be no harm.", "Do not indulge the cunning who only comply; beware of entangling alliances.", "Check robbery and cruelty; do not let the right way be overturned.", "O king, I wish to make you complete—thus I remonstrate aloud."], "dy-020": ["The Lord on High has grown perverse; the people below all suffer.", "What is said is wrong; what is planned does not look far.", "They ignore the sages and indulge themselves.", "They are neither loyal nor honest.", "Plans still do not look far—thus I remonstrate aloud.", "Heaven is sending down trouble—do not be so blithely glad.", "Heaven is in turmoil—do not chatter on so emptily.", "When words are harmonious, the people grow harmonious.", "When words are gentle, the people grow settled.", "Though our offices differ, you and I are colleagues alike.", "I come to counsel with you; you hear me with arrogant bluster.", "My words are solid—do not take them as a joke.", "The former people had a saying: ask even the grass-cutters and wood-gatherers.", "Heaven is being cruel—do not make sport like that.", "This old man is earnest and sincere; you young ones are proud and self-satisfied.", "It is not that I speak like a doddering elder—it is that you treat trouble as a jest.", "Much misconduct will blaze like fire, beyond remedy.", "Heaven is angry.", "Do not fawn and yield.", "All dignified bearing is in confusion; good men sit like corpses, doing nothing.", "The people are groaning in pain—does no one dare read the times?", "Death and disorder have spent our stores—and still no one shows kindness to our multitudes?", "Heaven guides the people like xun and chi in harmony, like zhang and gui fitting together, as easy as taking and leading by the hand.", "To lead by the hand needs no talk of adding more; guiding the people is easy.", "The people already lean toward crooked ways—do not yourself set up crooked laws.", "Good men are the hedge, the masses the wall, great states the screen, the great clan the pillar; cherish virtue and there is peace; the heir of the clan is the citadel.", "Do not let the citadel be ruined; do not fall alone into fear.", "Revere Heaven's anger; dare not make sport.", "Revere Heaven's change; dare not race about at will.", "Vast Heaven is said to be bright—yet it comes and goes with you as king.", "Vast Heaven is said to be dawning clear—yet it roams and indulges with you."], "dy-021": ["The vast Lord on High is lord of the people below.", "The violent Lord on High—his commands are often crooked.", "Heaven gave birth to the multitudes; their allotted nature cannot be wholly trusted.", "All have a beginning; few can reach a good end.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "How can you be so overbearing?", "How can you so fleece and strip?", "How can you sit thus in power?", "How can you hold office thus?", "Heaven sent down an arrogant temper, and you force it still higher.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "If you employ the good, the overbearing grow full of resentment.", "You answer with rumors.", "Bandits and plunderers operate inside the court.", "Cursing and praying without end.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "You roar and swagger in the central realm.", "You take the hatred you have drawn as virtue.", "Your virtue is not bright—thus you have no aides at back or side.", "Your virtue is not bright—thus you have no companions, no ministers.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "Heaven did not make you drown in wine, yet unjust deeds you follow and copy.", "Your bearing and conduct have already gone wrong.", "You make no distinction of day and night.", "You shout and you cry.", "You treat daylight as night.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "Like cicadas and locusts in clamor, like a boiling stew in turmoil.", "Great and small draw near to ruin, yet people still go on as before.", "Within you enrage the central realm; it stretches even to the Guifang.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "It is not that the Lord on High is unkind—Yin would not use the old ways.", "Though there are no seasoned elders, there are still statutes and penal codes.", "Yet no one heeds them—and so the great mandate topples.", "King Wen said, Alas—alas for you, Yin Shang.", "People have a saying: when the tree falls and roots are laid bare, the leaves are not yet harmed, but the root is already torn out.", "Yin's mirror is not far—it lies in the age of the Xia kings."], "dy-022": ["Strict dignified bearing is the squared edge of virtue.", "People have a saying: there is no wise man who never seems foolish; a commoner's folly is only the fault of his station.", "When a wise man seems foolish, he is offending common sense.", "Strongest of all is winning people; the four quarters will take him as their rule.", "With upright virtue, the four states will all submit.", "Great plans fix the mandate; far-sighted counsel is declared in due time.", "Revere your dignified bearing—it is the people's standard.", "But now you are lost in the business of government.", "You overturn your virtue and drown in wine.", "Though you follow pleasure, you do not think of the inherited charge.", "You do not seek widely the way of the former kings, to hold fast the clear law.", "Thus August Heaven does not protect you; like that spring flowing away—do not lead one another into ruin.", "Rise early, sleep late, sweep the courtyard within—this is a pattern for the people.", "Repair chariots and horses, bows, arrows, and weapons, to prepare for war, to hold off distant barbarian tribes.", "Settle your people, keep your statutes carefully, to prepare against the unexpected.", "Be careful in what you say, revere your bearing—let all be mild and fair.", "A stain on a white jade tablet can still be polished away; a stain on these words cannot be taken back!", "Do not speak lightly; do not say 'anything will do'; no one holds down my tongue—once out, words cannot be chased back.", "No word goes unanswered; no virtue goes unrepaid.", "Be kind to friends, and to the common folk and the young.", "Sons and grandsons continue with care; the myriad people all defer.", "See how you associate with gentlemen, soften your countenance—then perhaps there will be no fault.", "Look into your inner rooms—still feel no shame before the spirit of the uncovered roof-corner.", "Do not say it is not conspicuous, that no one sees me.", "The coming of the spirits cannot be measured—how much less may one grow weary and slack!", "Cultivate and brighten your virtue; make it good, make it fair.", "Guard carefully your conduct; do not err against ritual.", "Do not overstep, do not injure—few will fail to become a standard.", "Another throws me a peach; I repay with a plum.", "That young ram grows horns—truly it confuses the young.", "A tough fine wood is fitted with silk strings.", "A mild and respectful person is the root of virtue.", "If he is wise, tell him good words and he will walk by virtue.", "If he is foolish, he will say instead that I overstep.", "The people each have their own thoughts.", "Alas, you young one—you still do not know good from bad.", "Not only do I lead you by the hand; I also point out the principle in words.", "Not only do I command you face to face; I also take you by the ear to speak.", "Suppose you say you are still ignorant—yet you already hold a child in your arms.", "If a person is not self-satisfied, who can know early and yet ripen late?", "Vast Heaven is very clear; yet living I have no joy.", "I see you muddled and dark; my heart is grim with sorrow.", "I teach you earnestly; you hear me with scorn.", "You do not use it as instruction, but turn it into cruelty.", "Suppose you say you are still ignorant—you already count as advanced in years.", "Alas, you young one—I tell you the old statutes.", "Listen and use my counsel, and perhaps there will be no great regret.", "Heaven is in hardship; the state is about to be lost.", "The comparison is not far; Vast Heaven will not err.", "Crooked is your virtue, driving the people into great distress."], "dy-023": ["Lush is that tender mulberry; shade beneath is even; stripping makes it sparse—and so this people below is harmed.", "Worry in the heart does not cease; bleak dismay fills me.", "Vast Heaven above—can you not pity me?", "Four strong horses; banners flutter.", "Disorder rises and will not stop; no state is free of chaos.", "Among the people no able men remain; all have met disaster and turned to ash.", "Alas, what grief—the state's fate is so perilous.", "The state's stores are spent; Heaven does not help me.", "Nowhere to halt—say I go, yet where can I go?", "What the gentleman thinks keeps no mind for rivalry.", "Who gave birth to this calamity that still sticks as a thorn of illness?", "Worry deep and thick; I think of my soil and halls.", "I was born out of season, meeting Heaven's great anger.", "From west to east, nowhere to settle in peace.", "I see much suffering; the frontiers are in grave peril.", "If plans are careful, the chaos will lessen.", "I tell you of pity and care; I teach you to rank the offices in order.", "Who can hold something hot in hand and not rinse it in water?", "How then can one turn toward good?—only lead one another into drowning.", "Like walking against the wind—breath itself is hard to draw.", "The people have a will to rise, yet are blocked and cannot reach.", "Love this farming; labor for the people who till in your stead and feed you.", "Farming alone is treasure—is eating by another's toil truly good?", "Heaven sent down death and disorder, destroying the king we had raised.", "It sent down these crop-pests; the harvest is wholly harmed.", "I grieve for the central realm—linked on until all lies waste.", "There is no strength left to look up to blue Heaven.", "This kindly lord is whom the people look up to.", "Set your mind to make plans clear; examine and carefully choose aides.", "That uncompliant one thinks himself good alone.", "He has his own heart and guts, driving the people all into frenzy.", "Look in that wood—the deer run in herds.", "Friends already slander one another; they do not help with goodness.", "People have a saying: advance or retreat, both land you in a trap.", "This sage can see a hundred li with his eye.", "That fool, instead, is wild with joy.", "It is not that one cannot speak—why this fear and dread?", "This good man seeks no advancement, works no schemes.", "That hard-hearted one is remembered and employed again and again.", "The people's greed for disorder—they would rather take poison themselves.", "A great wind has its channel; emptiness lies in the great valley.", "This good man acts in accord with goodness.", "That uncompliant one walks in filth.", "A great wind has its channel; the greedy ruin their own kind.", "Agreeable words get an answer; remonstrance is heard as if drunk.", "You do not use good counsel, but make me rebellious instead.", "Alas, you friends—do I not know, and yet make this song?", "Like that flying bird—sometimes even it is shot and taken.", "Having already sheltered you, you turn and threaten me.", "The people without a limit devote themselves to harshness and ready betrayal.", "They do what harms the people, and still fear they cannot do enough.", "The people's crookedness races to work evil with all their force.", "The people are not yet settled, and they specialize in banditry.", "When I honestly say it will not do, they curse me behind my back.", "Though they say it is not aimed at me—I have already made this song!"], "dy-024": ["The vast River of Heaven turns its radiance across the sky.", "The king said: Alas!", "What guilt have the people of today?", "Heaven sends down death and disorder; famine comes again and again.", "There is no spirit we do not sacrifice to; we do not spare the victims.", "Gui and bi jades are already spent—will you still not hear me?", "The drought is already too severe; stifling heat drones like insects.", "Pure sacrifices never cease, from the suburban altar to the palace temple.", "Above and below we pour wine and bury jade; there is no spirit we do not honor.", "Hou Ji cannot save us; the Lord on High will not descend.", "Wasting and ruining the land below—has it fallen squarely on me?", "The drought is already too severe; it cannot be pushed away.", "We toil in dread, as of thunder and lightning.", "Of Zhou's remaining common folk almost none are left.", "Vast Heaven, Lord on High—will you leave me nothing?", "Why do you not fear one another?", "The ancestors too will be destroyed.", "The drought is already too severe; it cannot be held back.", "Blazing and scorching, it cannot be quenched.", "I grieve alone—how can one say blessing can still be gained?", "The great mandate draws near its end; no one looks up or cares.", "Spirits of the host of dukes and former ministers—will you not help me?", "Father and mother, ancestors—why are you so hard-hearted toward me?", "The drought is already too severe; mountains and rivers stand bare.", "The drought demon runs wild, like blaze, like fire.", "My heart dreads the heat; worry scorches like smoke.", "Host of dukes and former ministers—will you not hear me?", "Vast Heaven, Lord on High—would you make me flee?", "The drought is already too severe; I strive in reverence to pray the drought away.", "Why afflict me with drought?", "I do not even know the cause.", "I prayed for the year early; sacrifices to the directional and soil altars were not late.", "Vast Heaven, Lord on High—will you not aid me?", "Reverently serving the bright spirits, there should be no regret and no anger.", "The drought is already too severe; we are scattered, without bond of friendship.", "Distressed are the many officers; sick with worry is the Grand Steward.", "The Master of the Horse, the Master of Instruction, the steward of meals and those at left and right.", "There is no one who does not give relief.", "We cannot stop the drought; looking up to Vast Heaven—how can the heart find rest!", "Looking up to Vast Heaven, the stars glitter faintly.", "Great officers and gentlemen—make your clear appeal felt; do not slacken.", "The great mandate draws near—do not cast away work already done.", "What I seek is not for myself alone.", "But to settle the many officers.", "Looking up to Vast Heaven—when will you kindly grant peace?"], "dy-025": ["The great Marchmount rises steep, piercing Heaven.", "The Marchmount sent down a spirit, and bore the Marquis of Fu and the Earl of Shen.", "The Earl of Shen and the Marquis of Fu are pillars of Zhou.", "The four states take them as a hedge.", "The four quarters are thereby made open and clear.", "Diligent Earl of Shen—the king had him inherit the charge.", "He built a settlement at Xie, to be a model for the southern states.", "The king ordered the Earl of Shao to fix the Earl of Shen's residence.", "Complete this southern realm; generation after generation hold its merit.", "The king ordered the Earl of Shen to be a model for the southern realm.", "Rely on the people of Xie to build your walls.", "The king ordered the Earl of Shao to order the Earl of Shen's fields.", "The king ordered the tutors and chamberlains to move his household retainers.", "The Earl of Shen's achievement was managed by the Earl of Shao.", "The walls began to rise; the sleeping temple was already complete.", "Once complete it was majestic and deep; the king rewarded the Earl of Shen.", "Four horses proud and strong; breast-hooks bright.", "The king sent off the Earl of Shen with a road carriage and team.", "I considered your dwelling—nothing is better than the southern land.", "I grant you a great gui tablet as your treasure.", "Go, royal uncle—the southern land is yours to keep.", "The Earl of Shen truly set out; the king gave him a farewell feast at Mei.", "The Earl of Shen returned south, sincerely bound for Xie.", "The king ordered the Earl of Shao to mark the Earl of Shen's borders.", "Provisions were made ready to speed his travel.", "The Earl of Shen, martial and fine, has already entered Xie.", "Foot soldiers and chariot drivers are at ease.", "All Zhou rejoices—there is a fine pillar.", "Illustrious Earl of Shen, the king's great uncle—in civil and martial arts alike a model.", "The Earl of Shen's virtue is gentle in kindness and yet upright.", "He pacifies these myriad states; his name is known in the four states.", "Jifu made this ode; its meaning is grand.", "The tune is fine—made as a gift for the Earl of Shen."], "dy-026": ["Heaven gave birth to the multitudes; there are things and there are rules.", "The people hold to constant nature and love this fair virtue.", "Heaven watches over Zhou; brightness is felt below.", "It protects this Son of Heaven and gave birth to Zhong Shanfu.", "Zhong Shanfu's virtue—gentleness and excellence are his standard.", "Fair bearing, fair countenance, careful and wary.", "He takes the ancient teachings as his pattern.", "He strives in dignified bearing.", "The Son of Heaven follows him; bright commands he has him proclaim.", "The king ordered Zhong Shanfu to be a model for a hundred lords, to inherit your ancestors, to protect the king's person.", "He issues and receives the king's commands—he is the king's throat and tongue.", "He proclaims decrees abroad; the four quarters then respond.", "The solemn king's commands—Zhong Shanfu carries them out.", "Whether states are good or bad—Zhong Shanfu discerns it clearly.", "Both wise and intelligent, he uses this to keep himself whole.", "Morning and evening he does not slacken, serving the one man.", "People have a saying: soft things they swallow, hard things they spit out.", "Only Zhong Shanfu neither swallows the soft nor spits out the hard.", "He does not bully widowers and widows; he does not fear the overbearing.", "People have a saying: virtue is light as a hair; few among the people can lift it.", "I weigh and consider—only Zhong Shanfu can lift it.", "They love him, yet no one can help him.", "When the robe-of-state office has a gap, only Zhong Shanfu can fill it.", "Zhong Shanfu sets out and sacrifices to the road-spirit.", "Four horses tall.", "The travelers are swift, always fearing they will not arrive in time.", "Four horses gallop; eight bells clang.", "The king ordered Zhong Shanfu to go east and build a city.", "Four horses strong; eight bells chime.", "Zhong Shanfu goes to Qi—may he return soon.", "Jifu made this ode, harmonious as a clear breeze.", "Zhong Shanfu longs with far thoughts; use this to comfort his heart."], "dy-027": ["Mount Liang is tall; Yu ordered it; the roads are broad.", "The Marquis of Han received the charge; the king himself appointed him: inherit your ancestors; do not discard my command.", "Morning and evening do not slacken; devoutly keep your office; my command may not be altered.", "Correct those who do not come to court, to assist your lord.", "Four horses tall, long and strong.", "The Marquis of Han entered court for audience, bearing a great gui, presenting himself to the king.", "The king granted the Marquis of Han: fine flags and sash insignia, bamboo-mat carriage screens and patterned yokes, black robes and red shoes, breast-hooks and engraved forehead-plates, leather screens and light furs, rein-rings of gold.", "The Marquis of Han set out and sacrificed to the road, lodging overnight at Tu.", "Xianfu gave him a farewell feast—a hundred jugs of clear wine.", "What were the dishes?", "Stewed turtle and fresh fish.", "What were the vegetables?", "Bamboo shoots and cattails.", "What were the gifts?", "A team of horses and a road carriage.", "Bian and dou vessels were abundant.", "The feudal lords feasted in joy.", "The Marquis of Han took a wife—niece of the King of Fen, daughter of Juefu.", "The Marquis of Han went in person to welcome her to Juefu's lane.", "A hundred carriages thundered; eight bells clanged; radiance was illustrious.", "The accompanying bridesides followed, numerous as clouds.", "The Marquis of Han looked back; splendor filled the gate.", "Juefu was very martial; there was no state he did not reach.", "Choosing a husband for Han Ji—none was more peaceful than Han.", "Han's land is peaceful: rivers and marshes broad, bream and xu fish fat, does in herds, bears and brown bears, wildcats and tigers.", "Fortunate to have a fine dwelling; Han Ji is at ease and has renown.", "That great city of Han was finished by the Yan host.", "Because the ancestors received the charge, he leads these hundred Man tribes.", "The king granted the Marquis of Han the Zhui and the Mo peoples.", "He receives all the northern states, and so is their senior earl.", "Build walls, dig moats; order acres and fix the registers.", "Present skins of the pi, red leopards and yellow brown bears."], "dy-028": ["The Jiang and Han surge and swell; the warriors' spirit rolls like a flood.", "Not for ease, not for pleasure—they come to chastise the Huai Yi.", "Our chariots are already out; our banners already set.", "Not for ease, not for leisure—the Huai Yi come arrayed and pressing.", "The Jiang and Han roll vast and wide; the warriors are martial and bright.", "They ordered the four quarters and reported success to the king.", "The four quarters are already pacified; the kingdom is nearly at rest.", "Now there is no fighting; the king's heart is thus at peace.", "By the banks of Jiang and Han the king ordered Shao Hu: open the four quarters, order my borders.", "Do not harm, do not press; make the kingdom a standard.", "Mark the borders and govern them, as far as the South Sea.", "The king ordered Shao Hu: come inspect, come declare.", "When Kings Wen and Wu received the mandate, the Duke of Shao was a pillar.", "Do not say I am a mere youth—model yourself on the Duke of Shao.", "Be swift and keen in great affairs; thus I grant you blessing.", "I grant you a jade ladle, and a vessel of black millet wine.", "Announce to the cultured ancestors; I grant hills, soil, and fields.", "Receiving the charge in Zhou, following the Duke of Shao's charge, Hu bowed and knocked his head: May the Son of Heaven live ten thousand years!", "Hu bowed and knocked his head, praising the king's goodness.", "He made an inscription for the Duke of Shao's finished vessel: May the Son of Heaven live ten thousand years!", "The bright Son of Heaven—his fair name does not cease; he spreads his cultured virtue and brings these four states into harmony."], "dy-029": ["Illustrious and bright.", "The king ordered his ministers: Nanzhong is the great ancestor; the Grand Preceptor is Huangfu.", "Order my six armies; repair my weapons.", "Both reverent and prepared, show kindness to this southern realm.", "The king said to the Yin clan: order Chengbo Xiufu to array the ranks left and right.", "Admonish my host: along the Huai banks, patrol this Xu land.", "Do not linger, do not delay; the three matters are already in place.", "Illustrious and tall—there is a majestic Son of Heaven.", "The king advances slowly and at ease—neither late nor idle.", "Xu's realm stirred in continuous unrest, shocking Xu's realm.", "Like thunder, like lightning—Xu's realm was shaken.", "The king rose in martial might, like tremor, like anger.", "He advanced his tiger officers; their roar was like a tiger's howl.", "He arrayed thick forces on the Huai bank, taking ugly captives again and again.", "He cut across that Huai shore—there the royal host stands.", "The king's host is numerous and dense, like flight, like high birds.", "Like the Jiang, like the Han, like the root of mountains.", "Like a river's rush—continuous and yet ordered.", "Unfathomable, invincible—they march in force against Xu.", "The king's counsel is indeed full; Xu's realm has already come to submit.", "Xu's realm has already assembled—this is the Son of Heaven's merit.", "The four quarters are already pacified; Xu's realm comes to the royal court.", "Xu's realm no longer defies; the king says we may return."], "dy-030": ["I look up to Vast Heaven, yet it shows me no kindness.", "Long unsettled, it sends down this great calamity.", "The states are not at peace; gentlemen and commoners cannot gather and settle.", "Crop-pests harm like disease; there is no end, no ceasing.", "The net of guilt is not drawn in; there is no recovery, no healing.", "Others have fields—you seize them instead.", "Others have people—you snatch them away.", "This one should be innocent—you arrest him instead.", "That one should be guilty—you let him go free.", "A wise man builds a city; a wise woman topples a city.", "Fair indeed that wise woman—truly an owl, a screech-owl.", "A woman with a long tongue is the stairway to calamity.", "Disorder does not fall from Heaven—it is born of a woman.", "You hear no teaching, no instruction—only draw near to women and eunuchs.", "You probe people with envy, harshness, and deceit.", "Slander begins in rivalry behind the back.", "Is it not said to be already extreme?", "Why do evil?", "Like a merchant seeking threefold profit—the gentleman sees through this.", "Women do not manage public affairs, yet they stop silkworm work and weaving.", "Why does Heaven punish?", "Why do the spirits not grant blessing?", "You set aside your great Di troubles, yet hate me.", "Neither good nor auspicious—your bearing is unseemly.", "The worthy say they are perishing; the state is sick and nearly spent.", "Heaven sends down its net—already very generous.", "The worthy say they are perishing—the heart is anxious.", "Heaven sends down its net—already very urgent.", "The worthy say they are perishing—the heart is grieving.", "The gushing threshold spring—how deep it is.", "This worry in the heart—did it begin only today?", "Not before me, not after me.", "Lofty Vast Heaven—nothing cannot be made firm.", "Do not disgrace the august ancestors; thereby save your descendants."], "dy-031": ["Compassionate Heaven is violent and fierce; Heaven heaps death and disorder down.", "It afflicts me with famine; the people all flee and wander.", "My dwellings and frontiers all lie waste.", "Heaven sends down a net of guilt; crop-pests brawl within.", "Confused, slanderous, failing office—chaotic and crooked—they truly mean to topple our state.", "They cheat and defame, not even knowing their own stains.", "We toil in dread; long unsettled; my office is much diminished.", "Like that year of drought, grass does not flourish—like floating weeds dried on the water.", "I look at this state—nowhere but collapses and ends.", "Past plenty cannot match those former days.", "Today's suffering is worse even than now.", "Those who ate coarse grain now eat fine rice—why do they not withdraw themselves?", "Instead they prolong this state of affairs still further.", "When a pool dries up, one does not say it began from the shore.", "When a spring dries up, one does not say it began from the middle.", "This harm is general, and grows still wider; disaster falls on me.", "Of old when the former kings received the mandate, there were such as the Duke of Shao—daily opening the state a hundred li; now daily the state shrinks a hundred li.", "Alas, what grief!", "People of today do not honor those of old virtue."], "song-001": ["Ah, the solemn Pure Temple—grave and harmonious are the illustrious assistants at the sacrifice.", "Throngs of able gentlemen hold fast to King Wen's virtue.", "They exalt the spirit in Heaven, and hasten keenly about the temple.", "Bright and continuing—so that no one ever grows weary of them."], "song-002": ["Heaven's mandate—ah, solemnly it moves without cease.", "Ah, how illustrious—King Wen's virtue is pure and one.", "Its fair favor overflows upon me; I come to receive it.", "Mightily favor and aid our King Wen; the great-grandsons sincerely carry it out."], "song-003": ["Clear and bright—these are King Wen's statutes.", "Begin the pure sacrifice; in the end there is success—this is Zhou's auspicious omen."], "song-004": ["Feudal lords of merit and cultured virtue—this blessing is granted down.", "Kindness to me without bound; sons and grandsons keep it.", "Do not practice great evil in your states; the king will honor you.", "Think on these great merits; inherit the order and make it shine.", "Strongest is winning people; the four quarters will all take them as rule.", "Most illustrious is virtue; a hundred lords will all model themselves on it.", "Alas—the former kings must not be forgotten!"], "song-005": ["Heaven made the high mountain; the Great King cleared it.", "He opened the way; King Wen made it peaceful and well.", "They went forth; Mount Qi has easy roads; sons and grandsons keep it."], "song-006": ["Vast Heaven has a fixed mandate; the two kings received it.", "King Cheng dared not take ease; morning and evening, with breadth and care, he laid firm Heaven's mandate.", "Ah, how bright!", "He gave his whole heart—and so settled all under Heaven."], "song-007": ["I cook and I offer—sheep and cattle—may Heaven aid us.", "Model on King Wen's statutes; day by day settle the four quarters.", "Great King Wen has already come to aid and enjoy the offering.", "Morning and evening I revere Heaven's majesty—and so I keep it."], "song-008": ["In due time he tours the states; Vast Heaven takes him as son, and truly aids Zhou.", "A slight show of awe—and none is not struck with dread.", "He wins over the hundred spirits, and the rivers and high mountains; the true king is lord.", "Bright and clear is Zhou; those in office are set in order.", "Put away shields and spears; store the bows and arrows.", "I seek fair virtue and spread it through these Hua-Xia lands; the true king keeps it."], "song-009": ["Resolute King Wu—none had stronger merit than he.", "Illustrious Cheng and Kang—the Lord on High gave them praise.", "From Cheng and Kang on, they possessed the four quarters throughout, discerning even the fine.", "Bells and drums boom; chime-stones and pipes clang; blessings descend in plenty.", "Blessings descend greatly; bearing is careful and grave.", "Already drunk, already full—blessings and prosperity come in return."], "song-010": ["Think of cultured Hou Ji, who could match that Heaven above.", "He settled our multitudes—none but your standard.", "He left us wheat and barley; the Lord's command nourishes all, drawing no line between this border and that.", "Spread the constant way through these Hua-Xia lands."], "song-011": ["Ah, officers and workmen—revere your public duties.", "The king grants you established law; come consult and deliberate.", "Ah, farm officers—it is late spring; what more do you seek?", "How shall the new fields and burned fields be tilled?", "Ah, the fair wheat—it will receive a bright harvest.", "Bright and clear Lord on High—at last grants a peaceful year.", "Order my multitudes: put away your spades and hoes; go together to see the reaping."], "song-012": ["Ah, King Cheng—he has already made his clear appeal felt among you.", "Lead these farmers; sow the hundred grains.", "Vigorously open your private fields, as far as thirty li.", "Also take up your plowing—ten thousand pairs tilling side by side."], "song-013": ["White egrets beat their wings, by the Circular College on the west.", "My guests arrive; they are already gathered at ease.", "My guests arrive; they are already gathered at ease.", "There, no one loathes them; here, no one grows weary.", "May they be diligent morning and evening, to keep lasting final renown."], "song-014": ["A rich year—much millet, much rice; also tall granaries, ten thousand million reaching the zi count.", "Make wine, make sweet brew; offer them to the ancestors and ancestresses.", "To match the hundred rites; blessing descends widely."], "song-015": ["There are blind musicians, blind musicians, in Zhou's courtyard.", "They set up bell-frames and chime-frames; carved teeth hold inserted plumes.", "Small drums, great drums, hanging drums; hand-drums, chimes, zhu and yu all ready.", "Once ready they play; panpipes and flutes are raised together.", "The sound booms; solemn and harmonious they ring; the ancestors come to listen.", "My guests arrive, and long watch the success."], "song-016": ["Fair are the Qi and Ju streams; in the deep many fish lie.", "There are zhan and wei, tiao, chang, yan, and carp.", "Used for offering, used for sacrifice, to aid great blessing."], "song-017": ["They come in harmony and ease; they arrive in solemn reverence.", "Assisting at sacrifice are the feudal lords; the Son of Heaven is grave and majestic.", "Ah, present the great victims; help me array the sacrifice.", "How great, august deceased father!", "Settle me, this filial son.", "Wise are the worthy; both civil and martial is the royal lady.", "Peace reaches August Heaven; he can make his heirs flourish.", "Grant me long life with marked brows; aid with many blessings—aid both the meritorious deceased father and the cultured mother."], "song-018": ["At the first audience with the king, they say they seek the statutes.", "Dragon banners bright and clear; harness bells ring centrally.", "Rein-leathers are adorned; beauty has fierce radiance.", "They lead to audience with the bright deceased father, to fulfill filial duty and to offer.", "To aid long life with marked brows, to keep forever—may the august grant many blessings.", "Feudal lords of merit and cultured virtue—settle them with many blessings; let brightness reach great fortune."], "song-019": ["There is a guest, there is a guest—his horses too are white.", "Followers numerous and dense; his traveling company is refined.", "A guest stays one night; a guest stays two nights.", "Give him hobbles; hobble his horses.", "Go ahead to see him off; left and right comfort him.", "Already he has grand dignified bearing; blessing descends with easy grace."], "song-020": ["Ah, great King Wu!", "None had stronger merit than he.", "Truly there was cultured King Wen, who could open the way for his heirs.", "The heir King Wu received it, defeated Yin, checked the slaughter, and at last completed your achievement."], "song-021": ["Pity me, this young one—misfortune has struck the house; I am alone in pain.", "Ah, august deceased father—through all ages I can fulfill filial duty.", "I think of this august ancestor, ascending and descending in the courtyard.", "I, this young one, am reverent morning and evening.", "Ah, august kings—I inherit the order and do not forget in thought."], "song-022": ["Consult me as I begin to govern; I follow this bright deceased father.", "Ah, how distant—I still lack experience.", "Help me draw near to him; continue planning the scattered affairs.", "I, this young one, cannot bear the many troubles of the house.", "I inherit above and below in the courtyard, ascending and descending in his house.", "Fair, august deceased father—thereby keep and brighten his person."], "song-023": ["Be reverent, be reverent—Heaven is clear; Heaven's mandate is not easy to keep.", "Do not say it is high above; it ascends and descends among its ministers and gentlemen, watching here every day.", "I, this young one, am not wise or reverent enough.", "Day by day there is achievement, month by month advance; learning accumulates toward brightness.", "Aid me to bear the heavy charge; point me to bright virtue."], "song-024": ["I will take warning, and carefully guard against later trouble.", "No one led the bees here—I sought the bitter sting myself.", "At first it was only that wren; in flight it becomes a great bird.", "I cannot bear the many troubles of the house; I am sunk again in hardship."], "song-025": ["We clear weeds and fell trees; the tilled soil is loose and moist.", "A thousand pairs till and weed side by side, toward the low ground, toward the field ridges.", "There are household heads and eldest sons, younger brothers and nephews and many followers, strong laborers and hired hands.", "The meal-carriers call tan-tan; fair are the women who bring food, dear the men who plow.", "Sharp is that plowshare; they begin to till the southern acres, sowing the hundred grains.", "Seeds hold life; one after another they break the soil.", "The choice shoots are sleek and fine; the seedlings stand even and neat; weeding never stops.", "Reaping is numerous and thronging; stacks are full and solid—ten thousand million reaching the zi count.", "Make wine, make sweet brew; offer them to the ancestors and ancestresses, to match the hundred rites.", "Fragrance rises rich.", "This is the glory of state and house.", "Pepper-scent is fragrant; the elders find peace.", "Not only is this moment this moment, not only is today today—from of old it has been thus."], "song-026": ["A sharp fine plow—begin to till the southern acres.", "Sow the hundred grains; the seeds hold life.", "Someone comes to see you, carrying baskets and ju, bringing millet meal.", "The rain-hat is woven of grass; the hoe is very sharp—used to pull out bitter greens and smartweed.", "When bitter greens and smartweed rot, millet and broomcorn flourish.", "Reaping sounds zhi-zhi; stacks stand dense and firm.", "High as city walls, dense as comb teeth.", "Thereby open the hundred chambers.", "The hundred chambers are full; wives and children are at peace.", "Kill this yellow ox, its two horns curved.", "To inherit, to continue—continuing the people of old."], "song-027": ["Silk robes bright and clean; wearing the cap in reverence.", "From hall to steps, from sheep to cattle, great ding and small ding, the rhinoceros-horn gong curved.", "Fine wine is mild.", "Neither loud nor arrogant—this is the elders' auspicious blessing."], "song-028": ["Ah, the glorious royal host—follow the way of lying low until the time.", "When the time grows purely bright, thus comes great aid.", "I proudly receive it; vigor is what the king has wrought.", "Then there are heirs employed—truly take you, Duke of Zhou, as the model duke and teacher."], "song-029": ["Settle the myriad states; repeatedly gain rich years.", "Heaven's mandate does not slacken—martial King Wu.", "He keeps his gentlemen and host, thereby ordering the four quarters, able to settle his house.", "Ah, clear in Heaven—August Heaven used him to replace Yin."], "song-030": ["King Wen has already labored; I ought to receive the charge.", "I set forth this work and think on it continually; I go seeking only peace.", "This is Zhou's Heavenly mandate—ah, think on it continually."], "song-031": ["Ah, how great is this Zhou!", "Climb that high mountain—little hills and lofty peaks; truly plan to meet the river spirits.", "All under Heaven gather at this time to respond and exalt.", "This is Zhou's Heavenly mandate."], "song-032": ["Fat strong stallions, in the distant suburban wilds.", "Speaking of these horses: there are yu and huang, black and yellow—driving with forceful thunder.", "Thought without bound—thinking how fine the horses are.", "Fat strong stallions, in the distant suburban wilds.", "Speaking of these horses: there are zhui and pi, reddish and qi-marked—driving strong and sturdy.", "Thought without end—thinking how gifted the horses are.", "Fat strong stallions, in the distant suburban wilds.", "Speaking of these horses: there are tuo and luo, liu and luo-spotted—driving on without pause.", "Thought without weariness—thinking how the horses rise in spirit.", "Fat strong stallions, in the distant suburban wilds.", "Speaking of these horses: there are yin and xia, dian and fish-marked—driving vigorous and strong.", "Thought without crookedness—thinking how the horses travel far."], "song-033": ["There are fat horses, fat horses—fat are those four yellows.", "Morning and evening at the duke's place; at the duke's place they discern and manage affairs.", "Egret feathers flutter; the egrets settle.", "Drums sound yan-yan; drunk, they rise to dance.", "Joy together!", "There are fat horses, fat horses—fat are those four stallions.", "Morning and evening at the duke's place; at the duke's place they drink wine.", "Egret feathers flutter; the egrets are in flight.", "Drums sound yan-yan; drunk, they go home.", "Joy together!", "There are fat horses, fat horses—fat are those four dark horses.", "Morning and evening at the duke's place; at the duke's place they feast.", "From this day on, year after year of rich harvest.", "The gentleman has fair emolument, left for his grandsons.", "Joy together!"], "song-034": ["Joyful is the Pan River—come pick that celery.", "The Marquis of Lu arrives; look at his banners.", "Banners flutter thick; phoenix-bells ring hui-hui.", "Great and small alike follow the duke as he goes out.", "Joyful is the Pan River—come pick that waterweed.", "The Marquis of Lu arrives; his horses are proud and strong.", "His horses are proud and strong; his voice is clear and bright.", "Gentle face and smiling—not anger, but teaching.", "Joyful is the Pan River—come pick that water-shield.", "The Marquis of Lu arrives; he drinks wine in the Pan Palace.", "Having drunk fine wine, may he be forever granted agelessness.", "Along that long road he subdues these throngs of the base.", "Solemn Marquis of Lu—revere and brighten his virtue.", "Revere your dignified bearing—it is the people's standard.", "Truly civil, truly martial—make clear appeal felt by the meritorious ancestors.", "None fail in filial reverence; he seeks this blessing for himself.", "Bright Marquis of Lu—able to brighten his virtue.", "Having built the Pan Palace, the Huai Yi then submitted.", "Valiant tiger officers present severed left ears at the Pan Palace.", "Keen in judgment like Gao Yao, they present prisoners at the Pan Palace.", "Throngs of able gentlemen can broaden the heart of virtue.", "Martial they march out, opening that southeast.", "Full and august—neither loud nor showy.", "They do not clamor in disputes; they present merit at the Pan Palace.", "Horn bows are bent.", "Bundled arrows are many.", "War chariots are very broad.", "Foot soldiers and chariot drivers do not grow weary.", "Having defeated the Huai Yi, they are very good and do not defy.", "Firm your counsel; the Huai Yi are at last pacified.", "That flying owl flutters and perches in the Pan wood.", "It eats my mulberries and keeps my fair tones in its breast.", "The awakened Huai Yi come offering their treasures.", "Great tortoises and ivory; great tribute of southern gold."], "song-035": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "song-036": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "song-037": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "song-038": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "song-039": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "song-040": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "gf-021": ["Those little stars twinkle, three and five in the east.", "Hurrying through the night on official business, morning and evening at work.", "It is only that our lots in life are not the same!", "Those little stars twinkle—they are Shen and Mao.", "Hurrying through the night on official business, still carrying quilts and curtains.", "It is only that our fate falls short of others'!"], "gf-022": ["The river has a side stream; that person went home and did not take me along.", "Not taking me along—later she will regret it.", "The river has a sandbar; that person went home and will not stay with me.", "Not staying with me—later she will grieve.", "The river has a branch channel; that person went home and will not come to see me.", "Not coming to see me—I can only whistle my song aloud."], "gf-023": ["In the wilds lies a dead roe deer, wrapped in white rushes.", "A maiden's heart stirs with spring; a fine young man goes to tease her.", "In the woods stand thickets of young trees; in the wilds lies a dead deer.", "Bound neatly with white rushes; the maiden is fair as fine jade.", "Come slowly, softly—do not touch my sash, and do not set the dogs barking."], "gf-024": ["How can it be so richly gorgeous, like the blossoms of the tangdi?", "How could she not be dignified and beautiful?", "That is the carriage of a royal princess.", "How can it be so richly gorgeous, blooming like peach and plum?", "She is the granddaughter of King Ping, the son of the Marquis of Qi.", "With what does one fish?", "With a fishing line of twisted silk.", "The son of the Marquis of Qi, the granddaughter of King Ping."], "gf-025": ["The reeds grow sturdy and strong; one arrow brings down five sows—what a Zouyu!", "The mugwort grows sturdy and strong; one arrow brings down five great boars—what a Zouyu!"], "gf-026": ["That cypress boat drifts along, floating with the current.", "My heart is restless; I cannot sleep, as if burdened with unspoken grief.", "It is not that I have no wine to wander and ease my mind.", "My heart is not a mirror that can take in everything.", "Though I have brothers, I cannot rely on them.", "When I go to tell them, I only meet their anger.", "My heart is not a stone that can be rolled about at will.", "My heart is not a mat that can be rolled up at will.", "My bearing is dignified; I will not be faulted or belittled.", "Grief presses quietly on my heart; I am resented by that pack of petty men.", "The hardships I have met are already many; the insults I have suffered are not few.", "I calm myself and think it over, then wake and beat my breast and weep.", "O sun, O moon—why do you take turns to wane and lose your light?", "The sorrow in my heart is like a filthy garment that will not wash clean.", "I calm myself and think it over, yet I cannot spread my wings and fly high."], "gf-027": ["Green robe, green robe—green outer cloth with a yellow lining.", "The sorrow in my heart—when will it ever cease!", "Green robe, green robe—green upper garment with a yellow lower skirt.", "The sorrow in my heart—when will I ever forget it!", "Green thread, green thread—arranged by your own hands.", "I think of the one who is gone; may I make fewer mistakes!", "Fine cloth and coarse cloth—wearing them feels cool as a breeze.", "I think of the one who is gone; she truly suits my heart!"], "gf-028": ["Swallows fly in pairs, their feathers uneven in length.", "This person is marrying and going far; I escort her deep into the countryside.", "I gaze and gaze until she is gone; tears fall like rain.", "Swallows fly in pairs, wheeling up and down.", "This person is marrying and going far; I see her a long way on the road.", "I gaze and gaze until she is gone; I stand and weep.", "Swallows fly in pairs, their calls echoing up and down.", "This person is marrying and going far; I escort her to the south.", "I gaze and gaze until she is gone; it truly wounds my heart.", "Zhongshi is trustworthy and reliable, her heart honest and deep.", "Gentle and virtuous, careful in cultivating herself.", "Mindful of the late lord's charge, she comes to encourage me, this lonely widow."], "gf-029": ["O sun, O moon—you shine upon the earth below.", "Yet there is such a person who no longer treats me as before.", "How can my heart be at peace?", "Will he not even spare a thought for me?", "O sun, O moon—you cover the earth below.", "Yet there is such a person who is no longer kind to me.", "How can my heart be at peace?", "Will he not even repay me?", "O sun, O moon—rising from the east.", "Yet there is such a person who has not a single kind word.", "How can my heart be at peace?", "How can one forget?", "O sun, O moon—coming forth from the east.", "O father, O mother—you raised me, yet I cannot see it through.", "How can my heart be at peace?", "He treats me with no regard for right feeling."], "gf-030": ["The wind blows fierce and violent; he laughs when he sees me, frivolous and mocking, while my heart is wounded.", "The wind blows and raises dust; he rarely deigns to come—when he stays away, my thoughts wander long.", "The wind blows under a dark sky, overcast all day; I wake and cannot sleep—may he sneeze and think of me.", "The sky is heavily overcast; thunder rolls and rolls; I wake and cannot sleep—may he think of me in his heart."], "gf-031": ["War drums boom and boom; soldiers leap eagerly in training.", "Others build the walls of Cao in the capital; I alone march south.", "Following Sunzi Zhong, we go to pacify Chen and Song.", "They will not let me go home; my heart is heavy with worry.", "Where shall we lodge? Where shall we rest?", "And where has the horse been lost?", "Where shall we look for it?", "Under that grove of trees.", "In life and death, parting and reunion, I once pledged myself to you.", "Holding your hand, I would grow old with you.", "Alas, we are too far apart; they will not let me return alive.", "Alas, we have been parted too long; the vow made to me is not kept."], "gf-032": ["A gentle wind comes from the south, blowing on the tender hearts of the sour jujube.", "The jujube hearts are young and delicate; how hard Mother has labored.", "A gentle wind comes from the south, blowing on the sour jujube now grown to firewood.", "Mother is wise and kind; I alone have no good virtue.", "There is a cold spring below the town of Jun.", "There are seven sons, yet Mother still toils.", "The yellow birds sing clear and sweet, their song lovely to hear.", "There are seven sons, yet none can comfort Mother's heart."], "gf-033": ["The male pheasant takes flight, slowly spreading its wings.", "My heart is filled with longing; I myself brought on this separation.", "The male pheasant takes flight, its calls echoing up and down.", "Honest gentleman—you truly weary my heart.", "Looking at the sun and moon, my thoughts stretch long.", "The road is so far—when will you return?", "You gentlemen do not know what virtue means.", "Without envy or greed, how could one not be good?"], "gf-034": ["The gourd leaves have turned bitter; the Ji River has deep places one can ford.", "Where the water is deep, wade through in your clothes; where shallow, hitch up your skirts.", "The Ji is full and overflowing; wild pheasants crow.", "Though the water is high it does not wet the axle; the pheasant calls seeking its mate.", "Wild geese call yong-yong in harmony; the dawn sun has just risen.", "If a man would take a wife, let him do so before the river ice melts.", "The boatman beckons to ferry across; others cross—I do not.", "Others cross—I do not; I am waiting for my friend."], "gf-035": ["The east wind blows gently; it is cloudy and raining.", "We should strive together in one heart; we ought not to grow angry.", "Gathering turnips and radishes—would one use only the leaves and discard the roots?", "Do not go back on kind words; I wish to live and die with you.", "I walk slowly, reluctant to go forward; something in my heart is unwilling.", "You see me off only a short way, only as far as the gate.", "Who says bitter greens are bitter? To me they taste sweet as shepherd's purse.", "You are happy in your new marriage, close as true brothers.", "The Jing looks muddy beside the Wei, yet where the water stills it is clear.", "You are happy in your new marriage and will have me no longer.", "Do not go to my fish weir; do not open my fish baskets.", "When I myself am not accepted, how can I care about what comes after?", "Where the water is deep, we cross by raft or boat.", "Where the water is shallow, we swim and wade across.", "Whatever the household had or lacked, I strove to manage it.", "Whenever neighbors met disaster, I crawled to their aid.", "You cannot love and protect me; instead you treat me as an enemy.", "Having blocked my goodwill, it is like goods that will not sell.", "In earlier days of fear and want, I shared hardship with you.", "Now that life is settled, you compare me to poison.", "I have savory pickled vegetables that can also see us through the winter.", "You are happy in your new marriage; you used me to get through the hard times.", "You are violent and fly into rages, dumping all the toil on me.", "You do not remember our former affection, when you once loved me."], "gf-036": ["It is dark, it is dark!", "Why have we not yet gone home?", "Were it not for the lord, why stand out in the dew!", "It is dark, it is dark!", "Why have we not yet gone home?", "Were it not for the lord's person, why sink into the mud!"], "gf-037": ["Kudzu vines on Maoqiu—how long their joints have grown!", "Uncles and elder brothers, why put it off so many days?", "Why sit still and not move?", "Surely you have companions coming with you!", "Why delay so long?", "Surely there is a reason!", "Fox-fur coats are fluffy; it is not that the carts do not head east.", "Uncles and elder brothers, no one will take pity on me.", "Small and lowly—people scattered and homeless.", "Uncles and elder brothers, you plug your ears and will not hear."], "gf-038": ["Drums boom jian-jian; they are about to dance the Wan.", "The sun stands at noon; he takes his place in the front row.", "How tall and powerfully built that man is, dancing the Wan in the lord's courtyard.", "Strong as a tiger, he holds the reins neat as silk ribbons.", "In his left hand a flute, in his right a pheasant plume.", "His face red as dyed ochre; the lord grants him a cup of wine.", "On the mountain grow hazels; in the lowlands grows licorice.", "Whom does my heart think of?", "That beauty from the west.", "That beauty—ah, a person come from the west."], "gf-039": ["That spring trickles and flows, pouring into the Qi.", "My heart yearns for Wei; not a day goes by without thinking of it.", "Beautiful sisters of my clan—let me consult with them awhile.", "I set out and lodge at Ji; the farewell drink is at Ni.", "A woman marries and goes far, leaving parents and brothers behind.", "I send greetings to my aunts, and to my elder sisters as well.", "I set out and lodge at Gan; the farewell drink is at Yan.", "I oil the axle and fit the linchpin, then turn the carriage and drive on.", "If I hurry to Wei, surely it will do no harm?", "I think of Feiquan and heave a long sigh for it.", "I think of Xu and Cao; my heart wanders far.", "I will drive out for a pleasure ride, to ease my sorrow."], "gf-040": ["I walk out through the north gate; my heart is heavy with worry.", "Poor and hard-pressed—no one knows my hardship.", "Enough, enough!", "This is Heaven's arrangement—what more can one say!", "Royal duties are assigned to me; state affairs are piled all on me.", "When I come home from outside, the household takes turns blaming me.", "Enough, enough!", "This is Heaven's arrangement—what more can one say!", "Royal duties press upon me; state affairs are dumped all on me.", "When I come home from outside, the household takes turns humiliating me.", "Enough, enough!", "This is Heaven's arrangement—what more can one say!"], "gf-041": ["The north wind is chilly; heavy snow swirls and falls.", "You who are kind and fond of me—let us go hand in hand.", "Still hesitating, still delaying?", "The matter is already urgent!", "The north wind howls; heavy snow falls thick and fast.", "You who are kind and fond of me—let us return hand in hand.", "Still hesitating, still delaying?", "The matter is already urgent!", "What is not red is no fox; what is not black is no crow.", "You who are kind and fond of me—let us share one carriage and go.", "Still hesitating, still delaying?", "The matter is already urgent!"], "gf-042": ["How lovely that quiet maiden, waiting for me at the corner of the wall.", "She hides so I cannot see her; I scratch my head and pace about.", "How charming that quiet maiden, who gives me a red flute.", "The red flute gleams bright; I delight in your beauty.", "She brings tender rushes from the pasture—truly fair and rare.", "It is not the rushes themselves that are fair, but that a beauty gave them."], "gf-043": ["The New Terrace gleams bright; the river is full and high.", "I hoped for a handsome husband, but got a toad-like freak.", "The New Terrace stands tall and open; the river spreads without end.", "I hoped for a handsome husband, but got an ugly fellow beyond measure.", "The fishnet was spread, yet a wild goose fell into it.", "I hoped for a handsome husband, but got a hunchbacked ugly man."], "gf-044": ["Two boys go aboard a boat; their shadows drift with the waves.", "My heart longs for you; my sorrow will not be still!", "Two boys go aboard a boat, drifting farther until they vanish.", "My heart longs for you—surely you will not meet with harm?"], "gf-045": ["That cypress boat drifts in the middle of the river.", "The youth with twin locks of hair is the one my heart desires.", "Till death I will not change my mind.", "Mother! Blue Heaven!—why will you not understand!", "That cypress boat drifts along the riverbank.", "The youth with twin locks of hair is my true match.", "Till death I will not change my mind.", "Mother! Blue Heaven!—why will you not understand!"], "gf-046": ["Tribulus grows on the wall; sweep as one may, it will not come clean.", "Words spoken in the inner chambers must not be spoken aloud.", "If they could be spoken, what came out would still be ugly.", "Tribulus grows on the wall; clear as one may, it will not be cleared.", "Words spoken in the inner chambers cannot be told in full.", "If told in full, the tale would run too long.", "Tribulus grows on the wall; bind as one may, it will not stay bound.", "Words spoken in the inner chambers must not be spread abroad.", "If spread abroad, what came out would shame people."], "gf-047": ["She who should grow old with her lord wears a hairpin set with six gems.", "Her bearing is dignified and graceful, like mountain and river; splendid robes suit her.", "But if your virtue is poor, what then can be done?", "Bright, so bright—that pheasant-painted court robe.", "Black hair like clouds; she scorns to use a wig.", "Jade plugs for the ears, an ivory hairpin, a clear white brow.", "How like a goddess of Heaven?", "How like a daughter of the Lord on High?", "Brilliant, so brilliant—that ceremonial dress.", "Over it fine gauze of kudzu, her summer undergarment.", "Your brows are clear and fair; your forehead and face are beautiful.", "Truly such a person is the beauty of the realm!"], "gf-048": ["Where shall we gather dodder?", "There in the land of Mei.", "Whom does my heart think of?", "Beautiful Meng Jiang.", "She meets me among the mulberries, invites me to the Upper Palace, and sees me off to the Qi River's edge.", "Where shall we gather wheat?", "North of Mei.", "Whom does my heart think of?", "Beautiful Meng Yi.", "She meets me among the mulberries, invites me to the Upper Palace, and sees me off to the Qi River's edge.", "Where shall we gather turnips?", "East of Mei.", "Whom does my heart think of?", "Beautiful Meng Yong.", "She meets me among the mulberries, invites me to the Upper Palace, and sees me off to the Qi River's edge."], "gf-049": ["Quails fly in pairs; magpies go two by two.", "This man has no good character, yet I still treat him as elder brother!", "Magpies go two by two; quails fly in pairs.", "This man has no good character, yet I still treat him as my lord!"], "gf-050": ["When the Ding star stands mid-sky, they start building the Chu palace.", "They measure the site by the sun's shadow and raise the halls of Chu.", "They plant hazel, chestnut, yi, tong, zi, and lacquer trees, later to cut for zithers and harps.", "Climbing that ruined mound, one looks out toward Chuqiu.", "One sees Chuqiu and Tang, and also the great mountains and high hills.", "Coming down, one inspects the mulberry fields.", "The divination said auspicious, and the outcome was indeed good.", "Good rain has already fallen; orders are given to the grooms.", "At clear dawn they hitch the carts and rest beside the mulberry fields.", "He is not only upright in person; his heart is honest and deep.", "There are three thousand tall brood mares."], "gf-051": ["A rainbow appears in the east; no one dares point a finger at it.", "A woman marries and goes far, leaving parents and brothers behind.", "Morning mist-rainbows in the west mean rain all morning.", "A woman marries and goes far, leaving brothers and parents behind.", "Yet there is such a person, thinking only of marriage.", "Utterly without good faith, knowing nothing of fate's proper order!"], "gf-052": ["Look—even a rat has a hide, yet this person has no dignity!", "If a person has no dignity, why not simply die?", "Look—even a rat has teeth, yet this person knows no restraint!", "If a person knows no restraint, what else is there to wait for but death?", "Look—even a rat has a body, yet this person has no manners!", "If a person has no manners, why not die at once?"], "gf-053": ["On the staff a yak-tail banner flies high, outside the suburbs of Jun.", "White silk borders the flag; fine horses, four in hand.", "That fine person—what shall I give him?", "On the staff a bird banner flies high, in the capital of Jun.", "White silk is woven in; fine horses, five in hand.", "That fine person—what shall I present to him?", "On the staff a pennant flies high, within the city of Jun.", "White silk is wound about; fine horses, six in hand.", "That fine person—what shall I tell him?"], "gf-054": ["I drive the carriage hard and fast, going back to mourn the Marquis of Wei.", "The road of driving stretches long; I arrive at Cao.", "Great officers cross mountains and streams in pursuit; my heart is troubled.", "Since you do not approve of me, I still cannot turn back.", "I see you are not so wise; my purpose is not far-fetched.", "Since you do not approve of me, can I not cross the river and return again?", "I see you are not so wise; my longing cannot be held back.", "I climb that hill to gather fritillary bulbs.", "Women are full of care and feeling, yet each has her own reasons.", "The people of Xu blame me; the crowd is childish and arrogant.", "I walk across the fields; the wheat grows thick and lush.", "I appeal to the great states—on whom shall I rely, to whom go?", "Great officers and gentlemen, do not reproach me.", "For all your hundred schemes, they are not as good as the road I myself must take."], "gf-055": ["Look to that bend of the Qi, where green bamboos sway graceful and lithe.", "There is a refined gentleman—as if cut and filed, as if carved and polished.", "Solemn and imposing, bright and distinguished.", "There is a refined gentleman—never to be forgotten.", "Look to that bend of the Qi, where green bamboos stand verdant.", "There is a refined gentleman—jade ear-plugs gleaming, gems at his cap-seams like stars.", "Solemn and imposing, bright and distinguished.", "There is a refined gentleman—never to be forgotten.", "Look to that bend of the Qi, where green bamboos grow dense as a mat.", "There is a refined gentleman—like gold and tin, like a jade tablet and a jade disk.", "Generous and easy, he leans on the double carriage rail.", "Skilled at witty talk, yet never too cutting."], "gf-056": ["He builds a hut and lives hidden by the mountain stream; the lofty man's heart is broad.", "Alone he sleeps, alone he wakes, alone he speaks—vowing never to forget.", "He builds a hut and lives hidden in the mountain nook; how at ease the lofty man is.", "Alone he sleeps, alone he wakes, alone he sings—vowing never to stray.", "He builds a hut and lives hidden on the high ground; the lofty man lingers at ease.", "Alone he sleeps, alone he wakes, alone he lodges—vowing to tell no one else."], "gf-057": ["The beauty is tall and slender, in brocade with a plain outer wrap.", "Daughter of the Marquis of Qi, wife of the Marquis of Wei.", "Younger sister of the crown prince, aunt to the Marquis of Xing; Lord Tan is her brother-in-law.", "Hands like tender rush shoots, skin like congealed lard, neck like a longicorn larva, teeth like gourd seeds, a square brow and curved eyebrows; her clever smile shows dimples, her lovely eyes glance and shine.", "The beauty stands tall; her carriage stops in the near suburbs.", "Four stallions proud and strong; red silk harness ornaments gleam bright.", "With pheasant-plume curtains she comes to court.", "Let the great officers withdraw early; do not let the lord grow too weary.", "The Yellow River's waters roll vast and mighty, roaring northward.", "Fishnets splash as they are cast; sturgeon and carp leap and splash.", "Reeds and rushes stand tall; Jiang brides in rich dress come as escorts, and warriors look mighty and imposing."], "gf-058": ["That fellow came grinning, carrying cloth to trade for silk.", "It was not really to trade for silk—he came to talk marriage with me.", "I saw you across the Qi as far as Dunqiu.", "It was not that I meant to delay; you had no proper go-between.", "Please do not be angry; let autumn be our wedding time.", "I climbed that broken wall and gazed toward Fuguan.", "Seeing no one come from Fuguan, tears streamed down.", "At last I saw him coming from Fuguan—then I laughed and talked again.", "You cast the milfoil and read the tortoise; the omens held no ill words.", "Come with your cart to fetch me, and take away my dowry.", "Before the mulberry leaves fell, they were glossy and thick.", "Alas for the turtledove—do not greedily eat the mulberries.", "Alas for a woman—do not lose yourself in a man.", "When a man loses himself, he can still break free.", "When a woman loses herself, there is no way out!", "The mulberry leaves have fallen, yellow and dropping.", "Since I married into your house, three years have been all bitter hardship.", "The Qi rolled vast and full, wetting the carriage curtains.", "The woman did no wrong; it was the man who changed his ways.", "A man without a standard is of two minds and many hearts.", "For three years as a wife, there was no household task I did not labor at.", "Rising early and sleeping late, I had not one day of ease.", "Once your wishes were satisfied, you began to treat me with cruelty.", "My brothers do not know the truth; they only grin and laugh at me.", "I calm myself and think it over; I can only mourn alone.", "We said we would grow white-haired together; by old age you have made me resentful.", "The Qi still has banks; the marshland still has bounds.", "As children we played together, talking and laughing in joy; the oath was earnest and clear—I never thought it would be broken.", "Broken, and I will think of it no more—let it be done!"], "gf-059": ["A slender bamboo rod, used for fishing in the Qi.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "The road is far; I cannot reach you.", "The spring source lies to the left; the Qi to the right.", "A woman marries and goes far, leaving brothers and parents behind.", "The Qi lies to the right; the spring source to the left.", "Her clever smile shows white teeth; jade pendants ring as she steps lightly.", "The Qi flows on and on; cypress oars and pine boats.", "I will drive out for a pleasure ride, to ease my sorrow."], "gf-060": ["Branches of the wanlan; the boy wears an awl for untying knots.", "Though he wears the knot-awl, he cannot understand me.", "He puts on a grown man's airs, his sash dangling and swaying.", "Leaves of the wanlan; the boy wears an archer's thumb-ring.", "Though he wears the thumb-ring, he is no match for me.", "He puts on a grown man's airs, his sash dangling and swaying."], "gf-061": ["Who says the Yellow River is wide?", "A single reed would be enough to cross it.", "Who says the land of Song is far?", "Standing on tiptoe I can see it.", "Who says the Yellow River is wide?", "It would not even hold a little boat.", "Who says the land of Song is far?", "I could reach it in a single morning."], "gf-062": ["Elder brother, how imposing—a hero of the realm.", "Elder brother holds a long spear, driving ahead for the king.", "Since elder brother went east, my hair is tangled as flying tumbleweed.", "Is it that I have no hair oil?", "For whose sake should I dress up my looks!", "I longed for rain, yet the sun came out bright and glaring.", "Thinking only of elder brother, I would gladly endure even a headache from longing.", "Where can I get the plant that banishes sorrow?", "I would plant it behind the north hall.", "Thinking only of elder brother wounds my heart with pain."], "gf-063": ["A fox walks slowly across the bridge over the Qi.", "My heart is troubled—that person has no trousers to wear.", "A fox walks slowly at the ford of the Qi.", "My heart is troubled—that person has no sash.", "A fox walks slowly along the bank of the Qi.", "My heart is troubled—that person has no clothes."], "gf-064": ["You give me a quince; I give you a fine jade ju in return.", "It is not for repayment—I want our friendship to last forever!", "You give me a peach; I give you a fine jade yao in return.", "It is not for repayment—I want our friendship to last forever!", "You give me a plum; I give you a fine jade jiu in return.", "It is not for repayment—I want our friendship to last forever!"], "gf-065": ["There the millet stands in rows; the sorghum seedlings are growing.", "I walk slowly, step by step; my heart is shaken and ill at ease.", "Those who know me say my heart is troubled; those who do not ask what I am seeking.", "O distant blue Heaven—what sort of person is this?", "There the millet stands in rows; the sorghum ears are forming.", "I walk slowly, step by step; my heart is as if drunk.", "Those who know me say my heart is troubled; those who do not ask what I am seeking.", "O distant blue Heaven—what sort of person is this?", "There the millet stands in rows; the sorghum grain has set.", "I walk slowly, step by step; my heart feels choked.", "Those who know me say my heart is troubled; those who do not ask what I am seeking.", "O distant blue Heaven—what sort of person is this?"], "gf-066": ["My lord has gone on campaign; the date of return is unknown.", "When will he reach home?", "The chickens have gone back to roost.", "The sun has set; sheep and cattle come down the slopes.", "My lord has gone on campaign—how can one not think of him!", "My lord has gone on campaign; one cannot reckon by days and months.", "When shall we be reunited?", "The chickens have perched on the wooden stakes.", "The sun has set; sheep and cattle gather and come home.", "My lord has gone on campaign—may he neither hunger nor thirst!"], "gf-067": ["The gentleman is beaming with joy; left hand holding the mouth organ, right hand beckoning me to the side room—how happy!", "The gentleman is merry and content; left hand holding a feather pennant, right hand beckoning me out to roam—how happy!"], "gf-068": ["The surging river cannot float away even a bundle of firewood.", "Those people will not stand guard with me at Shen.", "Longing, longing—in which month can I go home?", "The surging river cannot float away even a bundle of thorns.", "Those people will not stand guard with me at Fu.", "Longing, longing—in which month can I go home?", "The surging river cannot float away even a bundle of rushes.", "Those people will not stand guard with me at Xu.", "Longing, longing—in which month can I go home?"], "gf-069": ["In the valley grows motherwort, withered and scorched yellow.", "There is a woman cast off; she heaves a deep sigh.", "Heaving a deep sigh—how hard it is to marry.", "In the valley grows motherwort, sun-dried thin and dry.", "There is a woman cast off; she wails aloud.", "Wailing aloud—the man she married was no good.", "In the valley grows motherwort, dry even where the roots were wet.", "There is a woman cast off; she sobs and weeps.", "Sobbing and weeping—regret comes too late."], "gf-070": ["The rabbit walks at ease, yet the pheasant falls into the snare.", "When I was first born, there was still little trouble; after I was born, I met a hundred calamities.", "May I sleep and never wake to stir again!", "The rabbit walks at ease, yet the pheasant falls into the trap-net.", "When I was first born, there was still little corvée; after I was born, I met a hundred sorrows.", "May I sleep and never wake again!", "The rabbit walks at ease, yet the pheasant falls into the bird-net.", "When I was first born, there was still little forced labor; after I was born, I met a hundred disasters.", "May I sleep and hear nothing more!"], "gf-071": ["Trailing kudzu vines grow along the river's edge.", "In the end I am far from my brothers, and call a stranger father.", "I call a stranger father, yet he will not spare a thought for me.", "Trailing kudzu vines grow along the riverbank.", "In the end I am far from my brothers, and call a stranger mother.", "I call a stranger mother, yet she will not draw near to me.", "Trailing kudzu vines grow beside the river shore.", "In the end I am far from my brothers, and call a stranger elder brother.", "I call a stranger elder brother, yet he will not look after me."], "gf-072": ["That person has gone to gather kudzu—one day apart feels like three months!", "That person has gone to gather southernwood—one day apart feels like three autumns!", "That person has gone to gather mugwort—one day apart feels like three years!"], "gf-073": ["The great cart rumbles; the woolen cloak is green as reed-grass.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "I fear you will not dare to say yes.", "The great cart rumbles heavily; the woolen cloak is red as fine jade.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "I fear you will not dare to elope.", "In life we dwell in separate rooms; in death we shall share one grave.", "If you say I am not true, let this bright sun be my witness."], "gf-074": ["Among the hills are hemp fields—that is Zijie who stays behind.", "That Zijie who stays behind—may he come walking slowly.", "Among the hills are wheat fields—that is Ziguo who stays behind.", "That Ziguo who stays behind—may he come to eat.", "Among the hills are plum trees—that is the one who stays behind.", "That one who stays behind gives me a jade jiu pendant."], "gf-075": ["How well the black robe fits; when it wears out I will make you another.", "I go to your lodging.", "When you return, I will have a meal ready for you.", "How fine the black robe looks; when it wears out I will remake it for you.", "I go to your lodging.", "When you return, I will have a meal ready for you.", "How ample the black robe is; when it wears out I will sew you a new one.", "I go to your lodging.", "When you return, I will have a meal ready for you."], "gf-076": ["Please, Zhongzi—do not climb over my village wall; do not break my willow trees.", "Is it that I grudge the trees?", "I fear my parents.", "Zhongzi is worth longing for, yet my parents' words are also fearsome.", "Please, Zhongzi—do not climb over my wall; do not break my mulberry trees.", "Is it that I grudge the trees?", "I fear my elder brothers.", "Zhongzi is worth longing for, yet my brothers' words are also fearsome.", "Please, Zhongzi—do not climb into my garden; do not break my sandalwood trees.", "Is it that I grudge the trees?", "I fear people's idle talk.", "Zhongzi is worth longing for, yet people's idle talk is also fearsome."], "gf-077": ["Shu has gone hunting; the lane seems empty of people.", "Is it truly empty of people?", "It is only that none compares to Shu.", "Truly handsome and kind.", "Shu has gone on the winter hunt; no one in the lane is drinking.", "Is it truly that no one drinks?", "It is only that none compares to Shu.", "Truly handsome and agreeable.", "Shu has gone to the wilds; no one in the lane is riding.", "Is it truly that no one rides?", "It is only that none compares to Shu.", "Truly handsome and imposing."], "gf-078": ["Shu goes hunting, driving a four-horse carriage.", "He holds the reins neat as silk ribbons; the outer horses dance like dancers.", "Shu is in the marshland; torches are raised all at once.", "Bare-chested and bare-handed he fights the tiger, to offer it at the lord's place.", "Please, Shu, do not grow too used to risk—take care not to be hurt.", "Shu goes hunting, driving four yellow horses.", "The two yoke-horses lead in front; the two outer horses fly like wild geese in line.", "Shu is in the marshland; torches are lifted all at once.", "Shu is skilled at archery and skilled at driving.", "Now he reins the horses still, now he lets them gallop free.", "Shu goes hunting, driving four piebald horses.", "The two yoke-horses keep even pace; the two outer horses answer like left and right hands.", "Shu is in the marshland; the fire burns fiercely.", "Shu's horses slow down, his arrows grow few; he uncaps the quiver and puts the bow in its case."], "gf-079": ["The troops of Qing are at Peng; four horses in armor look magnificent.", "Two spears heavy with red tassels—they wander and soar by the river.", "The troops of Qing are at Xiao; four horses in armor look imposing.", "Two spears heavy with feather ornaments—they idle at ease by the river.", "The troops of Qing are at Zhou; four horses in armor look merry.", "Wheeling left and drawing blades right, the central army strikes a handsome pose."], "gf-080": ["The lambskin coat is glossy and soft—truly upright and fine.", "That person would rather die than change his principles.", "The lambskin coat is trimmed with leopard—most imposing and strong.", "That person upholds what is right in the realm.", "How bright the lambskin coat, its threefold ornaments shining.", "That person is a distinguished talent of the realm."], "gf-081": ["Walking along the great road, I seize your sleeve.", "Do not dislike me—do not cast aside our old affection all at once!", "Walking along the great road, I seize your hand.", "Do not discard me—do not cut off our friendship all at once!"], "gf-082": ["The woman says the cock has crowed; the man says it is not yet dawn.", "Get up and look at the night sky—the morning star still shines bright.", "Then go out flying to shoot wild ducks and geese.", "When you hit some, bring them back and we will cook them together.", "With the dishes ready we drink wine, and grow white-haired together with you.", "Zither and harp played nearby—nothing is not quiet and fair.", "Knowing you care for me, I give you my mixed pendants.", "Knowing you yield to me, I console you with my mixed pendants.", "Knowing you love me, I repay you with my mixed pendants."], "gf-083": ["A maiden shares my carriage; her face is like the hibiscus flower.", "Light as if about to take flight, she wears fine jade pendants.", "That beautiful Meng Jiang is truly fair and refined.", "A maiden walks with me; her face is like hibiscus blooms.", "Light as if about to take flight, her jade pendants tinkle.", "That beautiful Meng Jiang—her virtue is unforgettable."], "gf-084": ["On the mountain grows the fusu tree; in the lowland grow lotuses.", "I do not see a beauty like Zidu, but meet this arrogant fellow.", "On the mountain grows tall pine; in the lowland grows red knotweed.", "I do not see a good man like Zichong, but meet this cunning youth."], "gf-085": ["Fallen leaves, fallen leaves—the wind blows you.", "Uncle, elder brother—you sing and I will join you.", "Fallen leaves, fallen leaves—the wind carries you.", "Uncle, elder brother—you sing and I will answer you."], "gf-086": ["That cunning boy will not speak with me.", "Only because of you I cannot eat.", "That cunning boy will not eat with me.", "Only because of you I cannot sleep in peace."], "gf-087": ["If you kindly think of me, hitch up your skirts and ford the Zhen.", "If you do not think of me, are there no others?", "You crazy boy are truly crazy!", "If you kindly think of me, hitch up your skirts and ford the Wei.", "If you do not think of me, are there no other men?", "You crazy boy are truly crazy!"], "gf-088": ["How full and fair your looks, waiting for me at the lane's mouth—I regret I did not go to see you off.", "How strong and flourishing your form, waiting for me before the hall—I regret I did not go to keep you company.", "Brocade upper robe with a plain wrap; brocade lower skirt with a plain wrap.", "Uncle, elder brother—drive the carriage and let me go with you.", "Brocade lower skirt with a plain wrap; brocade upper robe with a plain wrap.", "Uncle, elder brother—drive the carriage and let me return with you."], "gf-089": ["The open ground by the east gate; madder grows on the hillside.", "Her house is very near, yet she seems very far away.", "Under the chestnut by the east gate stand orderly homes.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "It is that you will not come to me!"], "gf-090": ["Wind and rain are bleak and cold; the cock crows jie-jie.", "Now that I have seen my lord, how can my heart not be at peace?", "Wind and rain fall whistling; the cock crows jiao-jiao.", "Now that I have seen my lord, how can my heart's illness not heal?", "Wind and rain dark as night; the cock crows without cease.", "Now that I have seen my lord, how can my heart not be glad?"], "gf-091": ["Blue, blue is your collar; long, long is my heart.", "Even if I do not go, will you not even send word?", "Blue, blue are your jade pendants; long, long is my longing.", "Even if I do not go, will you not even come?", "I pace back and forth upon the city tower.", "One day without seeing you feels like three months apart."], "gf-092": ["The surging river cannot float away even a bundle of thorns.", "In the end brothers are few—only you and I.", "Do not listen to what others say; others are truly deceiving you.", "The surging river cannot float away even a bundle of firewood.", "In the end brothers are few—only we two.", "Do not listen to what others say; others are truly not to be trusted."], "gf-093": ["Walking out the east gate, the women are as many as clouds.", "Though many as clouds, they are not the one I long for.", "She in white clothes and a blue kerchief is the one who makes me happy.", "Walking out the outer gate, the women are as many as rush flowers.", "Though many as rush flowers, they are not where my longing rests.", "She in white clothes and a red kerchief is the one I can share joy with."], "gf-094": ["In the wilds trailing grass grows; dew drops round and fall.", "There is a beauty, clear-browed and fair of eye.", "We meet by chance—just as my heart desires.", "In the wilds trailing grass grows; the dew lies thick.", "There is a beauty, fair, clear-browed and lovely of eye.", "We meet by chance—and hide our joy with you."], "gf-095": ["The Zhen and the Wei flow vast and full.", "Young men and women hold orchid plants in hand.", "The woman says, Shall we go look?", "The man says, I have already been.", "Shall we go look again?", "Beyond the Wei it is truly wide and joyful.", "Young men and women tease and banter, giving peony flowers.", "The Zhen and the Wei run deep and clear.", "Young men and women crowd in throngs.", "The woman says, Shall we go look?", "The man says, I have already been.", "Shall we go look again?", "Beyond the Wei it is truly wide and joyful.", "Young men and women are about to tease and banter, giving peony flowers."], "gf-096": ["The cock has already crowed; the court hall is already full of people.", "It is not the cock crowing—it is the sound of flies.", "The east is bright; the court hall is already bustling.", "It is not that the east is bright—it is the light of the moon.", "Insects fly buzzing; I would gladly share dreams with you.", "The court assembly is about to break up—do not let people dislike me and blame you."], "gf-097": ["How swift your movements—we meet between the slopes of Mount Niu.", "Side by side we chase two great beasts; you clasp hands and praise my skill.", "How handsome and flourishing your looks—we meet on the road of Mount Niu.", "Side by side we chase two male beasts; you clasp hands and praise me as fine.", "How strong and robust your form—we meet south of Mount Niu.", "Side by side we chase two wolves; you clasp hands and praise my ability."], "gf-098": ["Waiting for me between gate and screen—white silk ear-plugs, plus fine jade like flower bloom.", "Waiting for me in the courtyard—green silk ear-plugs, plus fine jade clear and bright.", "Waiting for me in the hall—yellow silk ear-plugs, plus fine jade fair and excellent."], "gf-114": ["The cricket has entered the hall; the year is nearly at its end.", "If we do not enjoy ourselves today, the days and months will slip away.", "Do not take excessive ease—still think of your proper duties.", "Take joy without neglect; the worthy man stays alert.", "The cricket has entered the hall; the year is about to pass.", "If we do not enjoy ourselves today, the days and months will go by.", "Do not take excessive ease—still think of matters beyond your post.", "Take joy without neglect; the worthy man is diligent and quick.", "The cricket has entered the hall; even the service carts have stopped.", "If we do not enjoy ourselves today, the days and months will steal away.", "Do not take excessive ease—still think of troubles to come.", "Take joy without neglect; the worthy man is at ease and content."], "gf-099": ["The sun rises in the east—that beautiful person comes into my room.", "Coming into my room, she steps in my footprints.", "The moon rises in the east—that beautiful person comes inside my gate.", "Coming inside my gate, she steps in the footprints of my going out."], "gf-115": ["On the mountain grows thorny elm; in the lowland grows white elm.", "You have clothes, yet you neither wear nor drape them.", "You have carriages and horses, yet you neither drive nor race them.", "When you suddenly die, others will enjoy them.", "On the mountain grows kao trees; in the lowland grows niu trees.", "You have courtyard and inner rooms, yet you neither sprinkle nor sweep.", "You have bells and drums, yet you neither strike nor beat them.", "When you suddenly die, others will keep them.", "On the mountain grows lacquer trees; in the lowland grows chestnut trees.", "You have wine and food—why not play the zither every day?", "Use them for joy, use them to pass the long days.", "When you suddenly die, others will enter your rooms."], "gf-100": ["The east is not yet light; clothes are put on upside down.", "Turned this way and that—because the lord is summoning.", "The east is not yet dry of dew; clothes are again put on upside down.", "Upside down and right side up—because the lord is giving orders.", "Break willows to fence the vegetable garden; the madman stares.", "He cannot keep the hours of dawn and night, nor put the long court assembly in order."], "gf-116": ["The surging river—white stones show clear and chiseled.", "In white clothes with a red collar-edge, I follow you to Quwo.", "Now that I have seen my lord, how can I not be happy?", "The surging river—white stones gleam pure and bright.", "In white clothes with a red embroidered collar, I follow you to Hu.", "Now that I have seen my lord, what sorrow is left?", "The surging river—white stones shimmer and flash.", "I have heard there is an order; I dare not tell another."], "gf-117": ["The pepper plant's fruit multiplies to fill a whole sheng measure.", "That person—tall beyond compare.", "O pepper—your fragrance travels far.", "The pepper plant's fruit multiplies to fill a whole handful.", "That person—tall and honest.", "O pepper—your fragrance travels far."], "gf-101": ["The southern mountain rises high; a male fox walks slowly.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden marries by this way.", "Since she is already married, why still pine for her?", "Hemp shoes come in pairs of five; cap ribbons hang in pairs.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden sets out by this way.", "Since she is already on the road, why does someone still follow?", "How does one plant hemp?", "By laying out the fields across and lengthwise.", "How does one take a wife?", "One must first inform one's parents.", "Since they have already been informed, why still indulge her?", "How does one split firewood?", "Without an axe it cannot be done.", "How does one take a wife?", "Without a go-between it cannot be done.", "Since she has already been taken, why let her run wild to the utmost?"], "gf-118": ["Tightly bind the firewood; the Shen star is in the sky.", "What night is this tonight, that I see this fine person?", "You, oh you—what will you do with this fine person?", "Tightly bind the fodder; the Shen star is in the corner.", "What night is this tonight, that I see this chance-met person?", "You, oh you—what will you do with this chance-met person?", "Tightly bind the thorns; the Shen star faces the doorway.", "What night is this tonight, that I see this beautiful person?", "You, oh you—what will you do with this beautiful person?"], "gf-102": ["Do not plow that great field; the weeds grow tall and proud.", "Do not long for one far away; the mind labors in anxious toil.", "Do not plow that great field; the weeds grow thick and bristling.", "Do not long for one far away; the mind labors in painful care.", "How fair, how lovely!", "The twin tufts of childhood hair stand up!", "Not long after we meet again—suddenly he already wears the adult cap!"], "gf-119": ["There stands a solitary wild pear, its leaves lush and glossy.", "I walk alone, forlorn and solitary.", "Is it that there are no other people?", "It is only that they are not brothers of the same father as I.", "Alas for those on the road—why will they not draw near to me?", "When a person has no brothers, why will no one help?", "There stands a solitary wild pear, its leaves green and lush.", "I walk alone with no one to lean on.", "Is it that there are no other people?", "It is only that they are not kin of my clan.", "Alas for those on the road—why will they not draw near to me?", "When a person has no brothers, why will no one help?"], "gf-103": ["The black hound's bells ring; that person is handsome and kind.", "The black hound wears double rings; that person is handsome with fine sideburns.", "The black hound wears double chains; that person is handsome and capable."], "gf-120": ["Lambskin coat with leopard cuffs—yet toward us he is arrogant.", "Is it that there are no others?", "It is only for the old affection we once shared.", "Lambskin coat with leopard sleeves—yet toward us he is harsh.", "Is it that there are no others?", "It is only for the friendship we once had."], "gf-104": ["A broken fish basket on the weir—the fish are bream and kun.", "The Qi maiden has returned; her attendants are many as clouds.", "A broken fish basket on the weir—the fish are bream and silver carp.", "The Qi maiden has returned; her attendants are many as rain.", "A broken fish basket on the weir—the fish come and go freely.", "The Qi maiden has returned; her attendants are many as flowing water."], "gf-121": ["Bustards shake their wings shu-shu, perching on clustered oak trees.", "The king's business never rests; we cannot plant sorghum and millet.", "On whom shall our parents rely?", "O distant blue Heaven—when shall we have a place to settle?", "Bustards spread their wings shu-shu, perching on clustered sour jujube.", "The king's business never rests; we cannot plant millet and sorghum.", "What shall our parents eat?", "O distant blue Heaven—when will this hardship come to an end?", "Bustards fly in ranks shu-shu, perching on clustered mulberries.", "The king's business never rests; we cannot plant rice and grain.", "What shall our parents taste?", "O distant blue Heaven—when shall we have a normal life again?"], "gf-122": ["Who says I have no clothes?", "I have seven sets.", "Only none are like the clothes you made—comfortable and auspicious.", "Who says I have no clothes?", "I have six sets.", "Only none are like the clothes you made—comfortable and warm."], "gf-123": ["There stands a solitary wild pear, growing to the left of the road.", "That gentleman—will he kindly come to me?", "My heart delights in him—with what shall I offer him food and drink?", "There stands a solitary wild pear, growing at the bend of the road.", "That gentleman—will he kindly come to stroll?", "My heart delights in him—with what shall I offer him food and drink?"], "gf-105": ["Driving the carriage with a thin sound; bamboo-mat curtains and red leather.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden sets out at evening.", "Four black horses evenly matched; soft reins hang down.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden is cheerful and easy.", "The Wen River rolls vast and full; travelers throng in crowds.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden soars to and fro.", "The Wen River flows on and on; travelers hurry back and forth.", "The great road of Lu is level; the Qi maiden roams and plays."], "gf-138": ["Under a humble gate of a crossbar, one may rest and linger.", "The spring of Bi flows full and ample—enough to fill hunger.", "Must one eat fish only if it is bream from the Yellow River?", "Must one take a wife only if she is of the Jiang clan of Qi?", "Must one eat fish only if it is carp from the Yellow River?", "Must one take a wife only if she is of the Zi clan of Song?"], "gf-124": ["Kudzu covers the thorns; lian vines trail over the wilds.", "My beloved is no longer here—who will keep me company alone?", "Kudzu covers the sour jujube; lian vines trail over the graveyard.", "My beloved is no longer here—who will rest alone with me?", "How bright the horn pillow; how splendid the brocade quilt.", "My beloved is no longer here—who will see the dawn alone with me?", "Summer's long white days, winter's long nights.", "After a hundred years, I will return to his grave.", "Winter's long nights, summer's long white days.", "After a hundred years, I will return to his resting place."], "gf-106": ["Ah, how flourishing—tall and long of stature.", "A broad, handsome forehead; lovely eyes glance and lift.", "His steps are light and measured; his archery is excellent.", "Ah, how good his name; his lovely eyes are clear and bright.", "The rites completed, he shoots at the target all day; the arrows never leave the center—truly my fine nephew.", "Ah, how fair—clear-browed, lovely-eyed, and graceful.", "His dancing keeps the beat; his shots can pierce through.", "All four arrows return to the center—enough to ward off chaos of war."], "gf-125": ["Gather licorice, gather licorice, on the peak of Shouyang.", "The tales others invent—do not believe them yet.", "Cast them aside, cast them aside—treat them as untrue for now.", "The tales others invent—what can they gain?", "Gather bitter greens, gather bitter greens, at the foot of Shouyang.", "The tales others invent—do not agree with them yet.", "Cast them aside, cast them aside—treat them as untrue for now.", "The tales others invent—what can they gain?", "Gather turnips, gather turnips, east of Mount Shouyang.", "The tales others invent—do not listen to them yet.", "Cast them aside, cast them aside—treat them as untrue for now.", "The tales others invent—what can they gain?"], "gf-139": ["The pond by the east gate can soak hemp.", "That beautiful, virtuous Ji maiden—one may sing in duet with her.", "The pond by the east gate can soak ramie.", "That beautiful, virtuous Ji maiden—one may converse with her.", "The pond by the east gate can soak rush grass.", "That beautiful, virtuous Ji maiden—one may talk with her."], "gf-107": ["Twisted kudzu shoes can walk upon the frost.", "A slender woman's hands can sew garments.", "She finishes the waist and collar; the beauty puts them on.", "The beauty is calm and self-possessed, gracefully turning left aside, wearing an ivory hairpin.", "Only because her heart is narrow do I compose this poem to satirize her."], "gf-126": ["There is the sound of carriages lin-lin; there are horses with white brows.", "Before seeing the gentleman, one only hears the eunuch pass the order.", "On the slope grow lacquer trees; in the lowland grow chestnuts.", "Now that I have seen the gentleman, we sit side by side and play the zither.", "If we do not enjoy ourselves now, people will grow old.", "On the slope grow mulberries; in the lowland grow poplars.", "Now that I have seen the gentleman, we sit side by side and blow the mouth organ.", "If we do not enjoy ourselves now, people will be gone."], "gf-108": ["In those low wetlands of the Fen, I go to gather sorrel.", "That person—beautiful beyond measure.", "Beautiful beyond measure, far unlike the highway officers.", "Along one side of the Fen, I go to gather mulberry leaves.", "That person—beautiful as flower blooms.", "Beautiful as flower blooms, far unlike the procession officers.", "At a bend of the Fen, I go to gather ox-lip herb.", "That person—beautiful as fine jade.", "Beautiful as fine jade, far unlike the clan officers."], "gf-127": ["Four iron-dark horses are sleek and strong; six reins are held in hand.", "Those favored by the lord follow him on the winter hunt.", "They present the season's male beasts; the season's male beasts are fat and large.", "The lord says, To the left—release the arrow and you will hit.", "They hunt and roam in the north park; the four horses are already well trained.", "Light carriages with luan bells and bits carry the xian and xiejiao hounds."], "gf-140": ["Poplars by the east gate—leaves rustle sha-sha.", "We agreed to meet at dusk, yet the morning star already blazes.", "Poplars by the east gate—leaves grow dense and lush.", "We agreed to meet at dusk, yet the morning star already shines bright."], "gf-128": ["A small war-cart with a shallow body; five leather straps bind the shaft.", "Sliding rings and side-drivers; breast-straps with white-bronze continuing rings.", "Patterned cushion-mats and long hubs; I drive my blue-black white-hoofed horses.", "I think of that gentleman, mild as fine jade.", "He is in that plank hut, stirring the depths of my heart.", "Four stallions sleek and strong; six reins held in hand.", "Blue-black and red horses in the middle; yellow-black horses as outriders.", "Dragon-patterned shields joined together; white-bronze rings fasten the reins.", "I think of that gentleman, mild and kind in the border town.", "When is the date of return set?", "Why make me long so deeply!", "Armored four horses move in harmony; three-cornered spears with white-bronze butts.", "Shields painted with patterns; tiger-skin quivers and gold-inlaid breast-bands.", "Two bows crossed and thrust in; bamboo bow-frames bound with cord.", "I think of that gentleman—I sleep, then rise again.", "That easy, fine person—his virtuous words are orderly and clear."], "gf-109": ["In the garden stands a peach tree; its fruit can make a dish.", "My heart is troubled—I sing songs and chant ballads.", "Those who do not know me say this scholar is too proud.", "Are those people right—what do you say one should do?", "My heart is troubled—who knows it?", "Who knows it? Better not to think of it at all!", "In the garden stands a sour jujube; its fruit can be eaten.", "My heart is troubled—let me walk awhile through the capital.", "Those who do not know me say this scholar has no standard.", "Are those people right—what do you say one should do?", "My heart is troubled—who knows it?", "Who knows it? Better not to think of it at all!"], "gf-141": ["By the grave gate grows a sour jujube; take an axe and cut it.", "That person is no good—the people of the state know it.", "Knowing it, he still will not change; it has always been so.", "By the grave gate grows a plum; an owl perches upon it.", "That person is no good—I warn him with a song.", "Warned, he still pays no heed; only in ruin will he think of me."], "gf-129": ["Reeds grow gray and dense; white dew has hardened into frost.", "The one of whom I speak is on that side of the water.", "Going upstream to seek him, the way is blocked and long.", "Going downstream to seek him, he seems to be in midstream.", "Reeds grow lush and green; white dew is not yet dry.", "The one of whom I speak is on the water's bank.", "Going upstream to seek him, the way is blocked and rising.", "Going downstream to seek him, he seems to be on an islet in the water.", "Reeds grow thick and flourishing; white dew has not yet ceased.", "The one of whom I speak is at the water's end.", "Going upstream to seek him, the way is blocked and winding.", "Going downstream to seek him, he seems to be on a sandbar in the water."], "gf-110": ["I climb that wooded mountain and gaze afar toward my father.", "Father says: Alas!", "My son has gone on service, morning and evening without rest.", "Be sure to take care—and still come back!", "Do not linger and fail to return!", "I climb that bare mountain and gaze afar toward my mother.", "Mother says: Alas!", "My little son has gone on service, morning and evening unable to sleep in peace.", "Be sure to take care—and still come back!", "Do not cast us aside and forget!", "I climb that ridge and gaze afar toward my elder brother.", "Elder brother says: Alas!", "My younger brother has gone on service; morning and evening he must keep companions.", "Be sure to take care—and still come back!", "Do not die out there!"], "gf-142": ["On the dike a magpie nests; on the hill grows fair tiao grass.", "Who is deceiving my beloved?", "My heart is troubled with anxious care.", "On the courtyard path lie tiles and bricks; on the hill grows fair yi grass.", "Who is deceiving my beloved?", "My heart is fearful and alarmed."], "gf-130": ["What is there on Mount Zhongnan?", "There are mountain catalpas and plum trees.", "The gentleman arrives here, wearing brocade and fox fur.", "His face red as if painted with cinnabar—truly a lord and king!", "What is there on Mount Zhongnan?", "There are foundations and broad level places.", "The gentleman arrives here, wearing embroidered robes and patterned skirts.", "Jade pendants ring jiang-jiang—long life that one cannot forget!"], "gf-111": ["Among the ten acres of mulberry fields the pickers are at ease—come, let us go home together.", "Beyond the ten acres of mulberry fields the pickers wander free—come, let us leave together."], "gf-143": ["The moon comes out bright and pure—how fair that beauty is.", "Her form is graceful and unhurried; longing fills the heart with sorrow.", "The moon comes out white and gleaming—how charming that beauty is.", "Her form is easy and composed; longing fills the heart with turmoil.", "The moon comes out shining—how radiant that beauty is.", "Her form is lithe and unhurried; longing fills the heart with bleakness."], "gf-131": ["Yellow birds call jiao-jiao, perching on the sour jujube.", "Who goes to be buried with Duke Mu?", "It is Ziju Yanxi.", "This Yanxi is a hero among a hundred men.", "Nearing the grave pit, he trembles with fear.", "Blue Heaven, Blue Heaven—you are killing our good man!", "If he could be redeemed, I would give a hundred lives for his one!", "Yellow birds call jiao-jiao, perching on the mulberry.", "Who goes to be buried with Duke Mu?", "It is Ziju Zhonghang.", "This Zhonghang is a shield among a hundred men.", "Nearing the grave pit, he trembles with fear.", "Blue Heaven, Blue Heaven—you are killing our good man!", "If he could be redeemed, I would give a hundred lives for his one!", "Yellow birds call jiao-jiao, perching on the thorn tree.", "Who goes to be buried with Duke Mu?", "It is Ziju Qianhu.", "This Qianhu is a defender among a hundred men.", "Nearing the grave pit, he trembles with fear.", "Blue Heaven, Blue Heaven—you are killing our good man!", "If he could be redeemed, I would give a hundred lives for his one!"], "gf-112": ["Chop, chop we cut the sandalwood and lay it on the riverbank.", "The river runs clear with rippling waves.", "You neither plow nor harvest—why take away three hundred chan of grain?", "You neither hunt in winter nor chase game—why do we see a huan hanging in your courtyard?", "Those gentlemen—surely they do not eat for nothing!", "Chop, chop we cut spokes and lay them by the riverside.", "The river runs clear and straight.", "You neither plow nor harvest—why take away three hundred yi of grain?", "You neither hunt in winter nor chase game—why do we see great beasts hanging in your courtyard?", "Those gentlemen—surely they do not eat for nothing!", "Chop, chop we cut wheels and lay them on the river shore.", "The river runs clear with little waves.", "You neither plow nor harvest—why take away three hundred qun of grain?", "You neither hunt in winter nor chase game—why do we see quails hanging in your courtyard?", "Those gentlemen—surely they do not eat for nothing!"], "gf-132": ["A swift zhan bird flies past the dense northern woods.", "Not seeing my lord, my heart is troubled with longing.", "What to do, what to do—how often you forget me!", "On the mountain grow clustered oaks; in the lowland grow red plums.", "Not seeing my lord, my heart is troubled and joyless.", "What to do, what to do—how often you forget me!", "On the mountain grow clustered di trees; in the lowland grow mountain pears.", "Not seeing my lord, my heart is troubled as if drunk.", "What to do, what to do—how often you forget me!"], "gf-144": ["Why go to Zhulin?", "To seek Xia Nan!", "It is not a special trip to Zhulin—it is to seek Xia Nan!", "Driving my four horses, I rest in the wilds of Zhu.", "Riding my little horses, I breakfast in the town of Zhu!"], "gf-133": ["Who says I have no clothes?", "I will share a war-cloak with you.", "The king is raising troops; I repair my dagger-axe and spear.", "With you I share the same hatred of the foe!", "Who says I have no clothes?", "I will share undergarments with you.", "The king is raising troops; I repair my spear and halberd.", "With you I will act together!", "Who says I have no clothes?", "I will share a lower skirt with you.", "The king is raising troops; I repair my armor and weapons.", "With you I will march forth!"], "gf-134": ["I see my maternal uncle off as far as the north bank of the Wei.", "What shall I give him?", "A great carriage and four yellow horses.", "I see my maternal uncle off; my thoughts stretch long.", "What shall I give him?", "Pendants of fine jade and precious stones."], "gf-113": ["Big rat, big rat—do not eat my millet!", "For years I have fed you, yet you will not spare a thought for me.", "I swear I will leave you and go to that happy land.", "Happy land, happy land—there at last is where I can settle.", "Big rat, big rat—do not eat my wheat!", "For years I have fed you, yet you will not feel grateful to me.", "I swear I will leave you and go to that happy state.", "Happy state, happy state—there at last is what I am due.", "Big rat, big rat—do not eat my seedlings!", "For years I have fed you, yet you will not comfort or reward me.", "I swear I will leave you and go to that happy suburb.", "Happy suburb, happy suburb—who there would still wail for long?"], "gf-145": ["On the bank of that pond grow rushes and lotuses.", "There is a beauty who wounds the heart till one knows not what to do.", "Waking and sleeping I can do nothing; tears and mucus pour down.", "On the bank of that pond grow rushes and orchids.", "There is a beauty, tall, with fine sideburns.", "Waking and sleeping I can do nothing; my heart is heavy and gloomy.", "On the bank of that pond grow rushes and lotus buds.", "There is a beauty, tall and dignified.", "Waking and sleeping I can do nothing; I toss and turn face-down on the pillow."], "gf-135": ["Alas for me—once the great halls ran deep; now each meal is finished with nothing left over.", "How sad—I cannot carry on as at the beginning!", "Alas for me—once each meal had four gui vessels; now each meal leaves me unfilled.", "How sad—I cannot carry on as at the beginning!"], "gf-146": ["In lambskin I roam at ease; in fox fur I go to court.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "My mind labors in anxious toil.", "In lambskin I soar about; in fox fur I stand in the hall.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "My heart is filled with sorrow.", "The lambskin is glossy as ointment; when the sun comes out it shines.", "Is it that I do not think of you?", "My heart mourns for this."], "gf-136": ["How you sway and toss on top of Wanqiu.", "Truly there is feeling—yet there is no hope.", "Dong-dong they beat the drums below Wanqiu.", "Winter or summer, always dancing with egret plumes.", "Dong-dong they beat the earthen jars on the road of Wanqiu.", "Winter or summer, always dancing with egret-plume banners."], "gf-147": ["Would that I might see the one in a white cap—gaunt to the bone—my heart restless with care.", "Would that I might see the one in white clothes—my heart is sad; I wish to return with you.", "Would that I might see the one in a white leather knee-cover—my heart is knotted; I wish to be of one mind with you."], "gf-137": ["White elms by the east gate; oaks on Wanqiu.", "The daughter of the Zizhong house whirls and dances under the trees.", "Choose a fine morning and go to the southern plain.", "She does not spin her hemp, but whirls and dances even in the marketplace.", "On a fine morning we go together, setting out in throngs.", "Seeing you fair as mallow, you give me a handful of peppercorns."], "gf-148": ["In the lowland grows the actinidia; its branches sway graceful, young and glossy—I envy your freedom from knowledge and care.", "In the lowland grows the actinidia; its blossoms sway graceful, young and glossy.", "I envy your freedom from household burdens.", "In the lowland grows the actinidia; its fruit sways graceful, young and glossy.", "I envy your freedom from family ties."], "gf-149": ["That wind howls and howls; that carriage races fast.", "Looking back along the great road, my heart is wounded.", "That wind whirls and whirls; that carriage speeds on.", "Looking back along the great road, my heart mourns.", "Who can cook fish?", "I will wash the pot and tripod clean.", "Who is heading west to return?", "Please take good news along."], "gf-150": ["Mayfly wings—clothes neat and bright.", "My heart is troubled—where is my resting place?", "Mayfly pinions—garments splendid and many-colored.", "My heart is troubled—where shall I rest?", "The mayfly emerges and transforms; hemp clothes white as snow.", "My heart is troubled—where is my resting place?"], "gf-151": ["Those waiting officers carry dagger-axes and spears.", "Those people—three hundred wear red knee-covers.", "The pelican perches on the fish weir; its wings are not even wet.", "Those people do not deserve to wear those clothes.", "The pelican perches on the fish weir; its beak is not even wet.", "Those people cannot long keep favor.", "Clouds gather dense—on the southern mountain a morning rainbow rises.", "Delicate and fair—yet the young maiden goes hungry."], "gf-152": ["The cuckoo is on the mulberry; it has seven young.", "The good and virtuous gentleman—his bearing is always the same.", "His bearing always the same, his heart firm as if set.", "The cuckoo is on the mulberry; its young are on the plum.", "The good and virtuous gentleman—his sash is of woven silk.", "His sash of woven silk; his leather cap has patterns.", "The cuckoo is on the mulberry; its young are on the sour jujube.", "The good and virtuous gentleman—his bearing has no fault.", "His bearing has no fault; he can be a model for the four quarters.", "The cuckoo is on the mulberry; its young are on the hazel.", "The good and virtuous gentleman can be a model for the people—a model for the people; why not enjoy ten thousand years?"], "gf-153": ["That cold downward-flowing spring soaks the clustered wolf-tail grass.", "I wake and heave a deep sigh, longing for that Zhou capital.", "That cold downward-flowing spring soaks the clustered mugwort.", "I wake and heave a deep sigh, longing for that capital of Zhou.", "That cold downward-flowing spring soaks the clustered milfoil.", "I wake and heave a deep sigh, longing for that royal city.", "Millet seedlings grow thick and lush; yin rain nourishes them.", "The four quarters have a king; Lord Xun comes to console them."], "gf-154": ["In the seventh month the Fire Star sinks west; in the ninth they issue winter clothes.", "In the eleventh month the cold wind bites; in the twelfth the frost is fierce.", "Without clothes, without coarse brown cloth—how shall we get through the year?", "In the first month we repair farm tools; in the second we lift our feet to the fields.", "Taking my wife and children, we carry food to the southern acres; the field officer is glad to see us.", "In the seventh month the Fire Star sinks west; in the ninth they issue winter clothes.", "Spring days begin to warm; the cangeng birds call.", "Girls carry deep baskets, walking the little paths to gather tender mulberry leaves.", "Spring days stretch long and slow; many go to gather white southernwood.", "A girl's heart is sad—afraid the young lord will take her home.", "In the seventh month the Fire Star sinks west; in the eighth they harvest reeds.", "In the silkworm month they prune the mulberries, taking up axes and hatchets.", "They cut the branches grown too tall and climb to pick the tender leaves.", "In the seventh month the shrike calls; in the eighth they begin to spin hemp.", "Dyed black and yellow—my vermilion is brilliant—to make clothes for the young lord.", "In the fourth month the far-will seeds; in the fifth the cicadas sing.", "In the eighth month comes the harvest; in the tenth the leaves fall.", "In the eleventh they go to catch raccoon-dogs, take fox pelts, and make fur robes for the young lord.", "In the twelfth they gather for the hunt and continue military drills.", "The little pigs we keep; the big ones we offer to the lord.", "In the fifth month locusts move their legs; in the sixth the shaji shakes its wings.", "In the seventh it is in the wilds; in the eighth under the eaves; in the ninth at the doorway; in the tenth the cricket creeps under my bed.", "We stuff the gaps and smoke out the rats, block the north window and plaster the door.", "Alas for my wife and children—saying the year is turning, we enter this house to dwell.", "In the sixth month we eat wild cherries and wild grapes; in the seventh we boil mallows and beans.", "In the eighth we knock down dates; in the tenth we gather rice.", "We brew this spring wine to help lengthen life.", "In the seventh we eat melons; in the eighth we pick gourds; in the ninth we gather hemp seeds, pick bitter greens and chop ailanthus for fuel—to keep us farmers alive.", "In the ninth we finish the threshing-floor garden; in the tenth we bring in the crops.", "Millet and sorghum, early and late, and also hemp, beans, and wheat.", "Alas for us farmers—when the harvest is put away, we must still go into town for palace work.", "By day we cut thatch; by night we twist rope.", "Hurry to mend the houses—then we must begin sowing the hundred grains again.", "In the twelfth they chip ice with a ringing sound; in the first they store it in the ice house.", "In the second they take ice for sacrifice, offering lamb and chives.", "In the ninth frost falls in the solemn sky; in the tenth they clear the grounds.", "Two jugs of wine for the feast—they say, Kill a lamb; ascend the lord's hall; raise the horn cup—ten thousand years without bound!"], "gf-155": ["Owl, owl—you have already taken my young; do not destroy my nest as well.", "Loving and hardworking, I raised my children with much pity.", "Before the sky turns cloudy and rains, I strip mulberry root-bark and bind the doors and windows.", "Now you people below—who still dares to bully me?", "My hands are already worn; I go to strip rush flowers.", "I store up thatch; my beak too is sick with weariness—and still they say I have no secure home.", "My feathers are scorched; my tail is withered; my nest teeters on the brink of falling.", "In wind and rain that rock and sway, I can only cry out in alarm!"], "gf-156": ["I went to the eastern mountains and long could not return.", "Coming back from the east, a fine rain falls misty and soft.", "In the east they said we would go home, yet my heart turned west in sorrow.", "I sew those casual clothes—no more marching with bits in our mouths.", "Writhing wild silkworms are many in the mulberry wilds.", "Alone I curl up to sleep, even under the war-cart.", "I went to the eastern mountains and long could not return.", "Coming back from the east, a fine rain falls misty and soft.", "Fruits of the gualou hang even to the eaves.", "Woodlice are in the house; spiders on the door.", "The field hut has become a deer yard; fireflies glow at night.", "It is not frightening—only that it makes one yearn.", "I went to the eastern mountains and long could not return.", "Coming back from the east, a fine rain falls misty and soft.", "Storks call on the earthen mound; my wife sighs inside the house.", "Sweep and block the rat holes—my campaign is nearly home.", "Round bitter gourds have long lain on the woodpile.", "Since I last saw her, three years have passed till now.", "I went to the eastern mountains and long could not return.", "Coming back from the east, a fine rain falls misty and soft.", "Cangeng birds take flight, their feathers flashing bright.", "When that person married, piebald and mottled horses drew the carriage.", "Her mother tied her sash for her; the rites were many and elaborate.", "The wedding was fine—and meeting again after long parting, how will it be?"], "gf-157": ["My axe is already broken, and my hatchet nicked.", "The Duke of Zhou's eastern campaign set the four quarters right.", "Pity us people—we too are quite remarkable.", "My axe is already broken, and my qi nicked.", "The Duke of Zhou's eastern campaign civilised the four quarters.", "Pity us people—we too are quite fine.", "My axe is already broken, and my qiu nicked.", "The Duke of Zhou's eastern campaign brought peace to the four quarters.", "Pity us people—we too are quite good and fair."], "gf-158": ["How does one cut an axe handle?", "Without an axe it cannot be done.", "How does one take a wife?", "Without a go-between it cannot be done.", "Cut an axe handle, cut an axe handle—the pattern is not far away.", "I meet this person; the bian and dou vessels are set in neat array."], "gf-159": ["Fish caught in the fine-mesh net are trout and bream.", "I meet this person, wearing a dragon robe and embroidered skirt.", "Wild geese fly along the sandbar; the lord returns with nowhere to lodge—stay two nights here with you.", "Wild geese fly along the land; the lord returns and will not come again—stay two nights here with you.", "Therefore leave the dragon robe—do not let my lord go back; do not make my heart sorrowful."], "gf-160": ["The wolf going forward steps on the dewlap; going back it trips on its tail.", "The ducal grandson is full of form; his red shoes stand firm and sure.", "The wolf going back trips on its tail; going forward it steps on the dewlap.", "The ducal grandson is full of form; his fair name has no blemish."], "xy-011": ["In the south there are fine fish; throngs catch them with cover nets.", "The gentleman has wine; honored guests feast and make merry.", "In the south there are fine fish; throngs catch them with scoop nets.", "The gentleman has wine; honored guests feast with delight.", "In the south there are bent trees; sweet gourd vines twine around them.", "The gentleman has wine; honored guests feast in quiet ease.", "Turtledoves flutter in, gathering here in flocks.", "The gentleman has wine; guests feast again and rejoice again."], "xy-012": ["On the southern mountain grow sedge grasses; on the northern mountain grow goosefoot greens.", "Happy is the gentleman—he is the foundation of the state and the house.", "Happy is the gentleman—may he have endless longevity.", "On the southern mountain grow mulberries; on the northern mountain grow poplars.", "Happy is the gentleman—he is the glory of the state and the house.", "Happy is the gentleman—may he have boundless longevity.", "On the southern mountain grow wolfberries; on the northern mountain grow plum trees.", "Happy is the gentleman—he is father and mother to the people.", "Happy is the gentleman—his fair name is passed on without end.", "On the southern mountain grow kao trees; on the northern mountain grow niu trees.", "Happy is the gentleman—how can he not live long?", "Happy is the gentleman—his virtuous reputation grows ever more lush.", "On the southern mountain grow ju trees; on the northern mountain grow yu trees.", "Happy is the gentleman—how can he not live to white-haired old age?", "Happy is the gentleman—may blessings guard your descendants."], "xy-013": ["Mugwort grows tall and long; clear dew moistens it.", "Seeing the gentleman, my heart opens in ease and joy.", "Feasting, talking, and laughing—thus there is fair renown and a secure place.", "Mugwort grows tall and long; dew falls thick upon it.", "Seeing the gentleman is like receiving favor, like seeing light.", "His virtue does not stray; his longevity is unforgettable.", "Mugwort grows tall and long; muddy dew clings to it.", "Seeing the gentleman, there is banquet joy and harmony.", "Fitting for elder and younger brothers alike—virtue, long life, and happiness.", "Mugwort grows tall and long; heavy dew gathers upon it.", "Seeing the gentleman—the hanging ornaments of his bridle sway gently.", "Luan bells ring in harmony; a myriad blessings gather together."], "xy-014": ["The dew is thick and heavy; without the sun it will not dry.", "The night feast is quiet and joyful; one does not go home until drunk.", "The dew is thick and heavy, falling on the lush grass.", "The night feast is quiet and joyful; bells are struck and music played in the ancestral temple.", "The dew is thick and heavy, falling on wolfberry and thorn.", "Illustrious, trustworthy gentlemen—none lack fine virtue.", "Paulownia and yi trees hang heavy with fruit.", "Harmonious, easygoing gentlemen—none lack graceful bearing."], "xy-015": ["The vermillion bowstring is loosened; accept it and store it well.", "I have an honored guest; inwardly I praise him.", "Bells and drums are already set; for a whole day we feast him grandly.", "The vermillion bowstring is loosened; accept it and load it on the carriage.", "I have an honored guest; inwardly I delight in him.", "Bells and drums are already set; for a whole day we urge wine and honor him.", "The vermillion bowstring is loosened; accept it and pack it in a bag.", "I have an honored guest; inwardly I cherish him.", "Bells and drums are already set; for a whole day we repay him with courtesy."], "xy-016": ["Artemisia grows lush and green, sprouting among the mountain bends.", "Seeing the gentleman brings joy and graceful presence.", "Artemisia grows lush and green, sprouting on the islet in the water.", "Seeing the gentleman, my heart rejoices.", "Artemisia grows lush and green, sprouting among the hills.", "Seeing the gentleman, he grants me gifts of a hundred peng coins.", "A poplar boat drifts along, now sinking, now floating.", "Seeing the gentleman, my heart can at last rest."], "xy-017": ["In the sixth month we are busy without rest; the war chariots are already put in order.", "Four stallions stand strong, carrying armor, uniforms, and banners.", "The Xianyun's arrogance is fierce, so we act with urgency.", "The king orders a campaign to set the kingdom right.", "Four black horses are chosen and matched; training follows the proper rules.", "In this very sixth month the military uniforms are already finished.", "Once the uniforms are ready, we first march thirty li.", "The king orders a campaign to assist the Son of Heaven.", "Four stallions grow tall; their heads are high and proud.", "Campaigning against the Xianyun, we establish great merit.", "Stern yet respectful, together we take on the military task.", "Together we take on the military task, to stabilize the kingdom.", "The Xianyun are no weak foe; they are entrenched at Jiaohuo.", "They invade Hao and invade Fang, reaching as far as Jingyang.", "Banners embroidered with bird patterns; white streamers flutter bright.", "Ten great war chariots go first to open the road.", "The war chariots are steady, tipping forward and back in due measure.", "Four horses are sturdy—sturdy and well trained.", "Campaigning against the Xianyun, we reach all the way to Dayuan.", "Jifu, both civil and martial, is the model for a myriad states.", "Jifu feasts with joy and receives many blessings.", "Returning from Hao, my days on the march have been long.", "Set wine to treat friends; cook turtles and slice carp.", "Who is seated there?", "It is Zhang Zhong, filial and friendly."], "xy-018": ["Go pick bitter greens—in that newly opened field, in this freshly plowed land.", "Fang Shu has arrived; war chariots number as many as three thousand.", "Shields and weapons are drilled; Fang Shu leads them.", "Driving four blue-black horses, the four stand in neat ranks.", "The great road carriage gleams vermillion; bamboo mats screen it, fish-skin quivers hang, hooks, breast-bands, and reins complete.", "Go pick bitter greens—in that newly opened field, here amid the countryside.", "Fang Shu has arrived; war chariots number as many as three thousand.", "Banners flutter bright and clear; Fang Shu leads them.", "Hubs bound with leather, crossbars painted in colors; eight luan bells ring qiang-qiang.", "Wearing the court robes, vermillion kneepads grand; green jade pendant rings clang.", "That swift falcon flies up to the high sky, yet will also settle down.", "Fang Shu has arrived; war chariots number as many as three thousand.", "Shields and weapons are drilled; Fang Shu leads them.", "The zheng-drum men strike; they array the lines and instruct the troops.", "Illustrious, trustworthy Fang Shu—drums boom yuan-yuan; the ordered host returns with a roar of tian-tian.", "Foolish southern Jing dare make enemies of the great state.", "Fang Shu is a senior statesman who can unfold great strategy.", "Fang Shu leads them, taking captives and seizing enemy crowds.", "War chariots rumble—their force like thunder and lightning.", "Illustrious, trustworthy Fang Shu campaigns against the Xianyun; the southern Jing also come in awe and submission."], "xy-019": ["My carriages are already repaired; my horses are already matched.", "Four stallions stand strong; we drive eastward.", "Hunting carts are ready; four horses stand tall and sturdy.", "To the east lie the grasslands of Putian; we drive there to hunt.", "Those men go to the summer hunt; the chosen followers bustle and shout.", "Raise the banners and set the yak-tail standards; chase game at Ao.", "Driving four stallions, the four horses are spirited and shining.", "Vermillion kneepads and golden shoes—allies at the assembly line up in order.", "Thumb-rings and arm-guards are ready; bows and arrows are tuned.", "The archers have gathered and help me pile up the game.", "Four yellow horses are harnessed; the outer side horses do not swerve.", "Driving follows the rules; every released arrow hits and pierces.", "Horses neigh xiao-xiao; banners drift you-you.", "Foot soldiers and drivers do not startle; the kitchens need not be piled too high.", "Those men return from the campaign—renowned, yet without uproar.", "Truly he is a gentleman; truly great merit is achieved."], "xy-020": ["The auspicious day is a wu day; we sacrifice to the horse ancestor and pray.", "Hunting carts are ready; four horses stand tall and sturdy.", "Climbing the great earthen mound, we chase herds of wild beasts.", "The auspicious day is gengwu; my horses are already chosen.", "Where the beasts gather, does throng in herds.", "Tracking along the Qi and Ju, we come to the Son of Heaven's hunting ground.", "Looking out over the plain, there are many great beasts.", "Some run, some walk—in herds or in pairs.", "Leading those left and right together, we let the Son of Heaven rest at ease and rejoice.", "I draw my bow and set my arrow.", "I shoot that small wild boar and bring down this great rhinoceros.", "With these we feast the guests and ladle sweet wine to drink freely."], "xy-021": ["Wild geese fly, fly—wings beat su-su.", "Those people go to labor service, toiling in the wilds.", "It reaches even the pitiful ones; pity these widowers and widows.", "Wild geese fly, fly—and settle in the marshes.", "Those people go to build walls; a hundred sections of wall rise.", "Though the labor is hard, at last they can settle securely.", "Wild geese fly, fly—crying out in mournful ao-ao.", "Those who understand say I am indeed hard-pressed.", "The foolish say I am showing off in pride."], "xy-022": ["What hour of the night has it reached?", "Night is not yet over; the courtyard torches burn bright.", "The gentleman is arriving; luan bells ring jiang-jiang.", "What hour of the night has it reached?", "Night has not yet faded; the courtyard torches shine clear.", "The gentleman is arriving; luan bells ring hui-hui.", "What hour of the night has it reached?", "Night nears dawn; the courtyard torches still glow with leftover light.", "The gentleman is arriving—his banners can now be seen."], "xy-023": ["That full-flowing water goes as tributary toward the great sea.", "The swift falcon flies and then settles.", "Alas for my brothers, friends within the state.", "None will attend to the chaos—who has no parents?", "That full-flowing water runs vast and rolling.", "The swift falcon flies and then soars up again.", "Thinking of those who do not keep the right path, I rise and pace about.", "The sorrow in my heart cannot be cleared or forgotten.", "The swift falcon flies along the mountain ridges.", "Rumors rise everywhere among the people—is there truly no one to punish them?", "My friends, be on guard—slander is about to arise."], "xy-024": ["The crane calls in the deep marsh; its voice reaches the open plain.", "Fish hide in the deep abyss, and at times are also on the shallow shoals.", "How lovely that garden is, planted with sandalwood; beneath the trees lie fallen leaves.", "Stones from other mountains can serve as whetstones.", "The crane calls in the deep marsh; its voice reaches the heavens.", "Fish are on the shallow shoals, and at times hide in the deep abyss.", "How lovely that garden is, planted with sandalwood; beneath the trees grow paper mulberries.", "Stones from other mountains can be used to polish jade."], "xy-025": ["Minister of War—I am the king's claw and tooth, his guard.", "Why push me into hardship with nowhere to settle?", "Minister of War—I am the king's claw and tooth, his warrior.", "Why push me into hardship with nowhere to return and rest?", "Minister of War—you are truly not wise.", "Why push me into hardship?", "At home an aging mother still waits for me to support her."], "xy-026": ["Bright white colt, eating the green shoots in my yard.", "Tie it, tether it, so we may keep this whole morning.", "That person of whom we speak—where is he roaming at ease?", "Bright white colt, eating the bean leaves in my yard.", "Tie it, tether it, so we may keep this whole evening.", "That person of whom we speak—where is he staying as a guest?", "Bright white colt, coming here with graceful ease.", "You are a duke, a lord—will ease and pleasure never end?", "Cherish your leisurely wandering; give up thoughts of withdrawal.", "Bright white colt, in that empty mountain valley.", "A bundle of fresh grass—that person is like fine jade.", "Do not treat news as precious as gold and jade, and so grow distant at heart."], "xy-027": ["Yellow birds, yellow birds—do not perch on the paper mulberry; do not peck my millet.", "The people of this state will not treat me kindly.", "If I say go home, then go home—back to my own clan.", "Yellow birds, yellow birds—do not perch on the mulberry; do not peck my sorghum.", "The people of this state cannot be allied with.", "If I say go home, then go home—back to my elder brothers.", "Yellow birds, yellow birds—do not perch on the oak; do not peck my millet grain.", "The people of this state cannot be lived with.", "If I say go home, then go home—back to my father's generation."], "xy-028": ["I walk through the wilds; the chu tree blocks out sun and sky.", "Because of marriage I came to live with you.", "If you will not keep and support me, I will return to my own state and house.", "I walk through the wilds to gather that zhu herb.", "Because of marriage I came to share your bed.", "If you will not keep and support me, I will go back and find another way.", "I walk through the wilds to gather that fu herb.", "You do not remember our old marriage bond, but seek your new love.", "It is not because she is rich—only that you tire of the old and love the new."], "xy-029": ["Stream water flows clear and cool; the southern mountains are deep and still.", "Rooted like a bamboo grove, flourishing like pine trees.", "Elder and younger brothers—be friendly to one another; do not deceive each other.", "Inheriting from former mothers and fathers, build a house of a hundred walls, with gates opening southwest.", "Here we dwell in security; here we laugh and speak.", "Binding the wall-boards sounds ge-ge; pounding the earth sounds tuo-tuo.", "Wind and rain are shut out; birds and rats are driven away—the gentleman dwells here.", "Like one on tiptoe spreading wings, like an arrow with sharp angles, like a bird opening its wings, like a pheasant in flight—the gentleman ascends upon it.", "The courtyard is level and spacious; the pillars stand tall and straight.", "The main hall is bright and open; the inner rooms deep and wide—the gentleman finds peace here.", "Rush mats below, bamboo mats above—then he lies down at ease.", "Having slept, he rises and asks about my dream.", "What is the auspicious dream?", "It is a bear, a brown bear; it is a viper, a snake.", "The grand diviner pronounces: bears and brown bears are omens of a son; vipers and snakes are omens of a daughter.", "If a boy is born, let him sleep on the bed.", "Dress him in a skirt; give him a jade zhang scepter to play with.", "His cry is loud and clear; vermillion kneepads grand—he will be lord and king of the house.", "If a girl is born, let her sleep on the ground.", "Dress her in swaddling clothes; give her a spindle-whorl to play with.", "Make no mistakes, take no unauthorized decisions—speak only of wine and food, and bring no worry to parents."], "xy-030": ["Who says you have no sheep?", "Three hundred make a flock.", "Who says you have no cattle?", "Ninety great yellow oxen.", "Your sheep come—horns densely clustered.", "Your cattle come—ears wet and flicking.", "Some go down into the mountain bends, some drink by the pond, some sleep, some move.", "Your herdsman comes, wearing a rain cape and bamboo hat; some carry dry rations on their backs.", "Thirty kinds of coat color and class—sacrificial animals are all complete.", "Your herdsman comes, gathering firewood and cutting grass, sorting female from male.", "Your sheep come, careful and orderly, neither lost nor scattered.", "At a wave of the arm they all follow and climb into the pen.", "The herdsman dreamed: the multitude became fish; turtle banners became bird banners. The grand diviner said: multitudes becoming fish means a rich year; banners becoming bird banners means the household will prosper."], "xy-031": ["Lofty southern mountains—rocks rise in sheer layers.", "Illustrious Master Yin—the people all look up to you.", "Anxiety burns like fire; we dare not jest or chatter.", "The state's fortune is already cut off—why do you not watch and inspect!", "Lofty southern mountains—slopes thick with plants.", "Illustrious Master Yin—what propriety is there without fairness?", "Heaven is sending down plague; mourning and turmoil are many and great.", "The people's complaints have no kind words, yet you look grim and do not punish.", "Yin the Grand Master is the pillar of the Zhou house; holding the balance of state affairs, you bind the four directions.", "Assist the Son of Heaven so the people are not lost and confused.", "Uncaring blue Heaven—you should not leave the people empty and depleted.", "If you do not personally inquire, the common people will not submit.", "Do not ask after or employ the worthy; do not deceive gentlemen.", "Calm the chaos and stop evil deeds; do not let petty men do harm.", "Trivial marriage connections of kinship are given heavy appointments.", "Blue Heaven is unfair, sending down this great calamity.", "Blue Heaven is unkind, sending down this great disaster.", "If gentlemen come into government, they can calm the people's hearts.", "If gentlemen are fair, resentment and anger will go far away.", "Uncaring blue Heaven—the chaos has not settled.", "Calamity grows month by month, so the people cannot have peace.", "Anxiety is like drunkenness—who is in charge of the state?", "You yourself do not personally manage affairs, and in the end leave the people toiling.", "Driving four stallions, the horses' necks are thick and strong.", "I look to the four directions—hemmed in, with nowhere to gallop.", "Just when your wrongdoing is at its height, all spears point at you.", "Once things settle they are glad again, as if urging one another to drink.", "Blue Heaven is unfair; our king cannot have peace.", "You do not chastise your own heart, but resent the upright instead.", "Jiafu composed this poem to pursue the root of the king's calamity.", "May you change your mind, and so nourish the myriad states."], "xy-032": ["In the first month heavy frost falls; my heart is sorrowful.", "Rumors among the people are also rampant.", "Thinking of myself alone, anxiety weighs heavy.", "I sigh that I am so careful, yet sickness and sorrow meet.", "Father and mother gave me birth—why make me suffer illness?", "Disaster does not come before me, nor after me.", "Kind words come from the mouth; harsh words also come from the mouth.", "Anxiety grows heavier and heavier; thus I suffer insult.", "Anxiety is lonely—I think how I have no salary.", "Innocent common people, even servants and retainers, suffer together.", "Alas for people like us—where shall we seek a livelihood?", "Look where the crows settle—", "On whose rooftop do they perch?", "Looking into that forest—some become firewood, some become grass.", "The people are now in peril; looking at Heaven, all is dim and dreamlike.", "Once Heaven's mandate is fixed, no one can overcome Heaven.", "August God on High—whom do you truly hate?", "They say the mountains are so low, yet they are ridges and mounds.", "Rumors among the people—is there truly no one to punish them?", "Summon those old veterans and ask about dream divination.", "All claim to be sagely wise—who can tell male crow from female!", "They say Heaven is so high, yet dare not but bend the waist.", "They say Earth is so thick, yet dare not but take small steps.", "Speak out these words—they have order and grounds.", "Alas for people today—why are they like venomous snakes and lizards?", "Looking at that slope field—there is a sturdy solitary seedling.", "Heaven shakes me as if fearing it cannot subdue me.", "When they seek me, they fear only that they cannot get me.", "Having got me, they hate and slight me, and do not employ me either.", "The sorrow in my heart is like a knotted tangle.", "Today's government—why is it so violent and harsh?", "The great fire blazes—can anyone put it out?", "Illustrious ancestral Zhou was destroyed by Baosi!", "Long nursing worry, further trapped by rain and gloom.", "The cart is already fully loaded, yet they throw away the axle-pin.", "Only when the goods are about to overturn do they cry, 'Uncle, help me!'", "Do not throw away the axle-pin; strengthen your wheel spokes.", "Always look after your drivers, and then the goods will not overturn.", "At last one can cross the danger—yet you pay it no mind.", "Fish in the pond also cannot find ease.", "Even when they hide, they are still quite exposed.", "Anxiety is bleak—thinking of the government's cruelty!", "They have fine wine and also fine dishes.", "Close ties with neighbors; marriage kin come and go in bustle.", "Thinking of myself alone, anxiety runs deep.", "Mean people have houses; low people have grain.", "The people now have no salary; Heaven sends disaster to crush them.", "The rich still get by—alas for these lonely ones with no one to lean on."], "xy-033": ["At the conjunction of the tenth month, the new-moon day is xinmao.", "The sun has an eclipse—also a great disgrace.", "That moon wanes faint; this sun also wanes faint; the people below now are also deeply sad.", "Sun and moon announce ill omens, not running their usual courses.", "The four directions have no good government; worthy and good people are not employed.", "When that moon is eaten, it may still count as ordinary; when this sun is eaten—why is that not good?", "Lightning flashes ye-ye—unsettled and not good.", "A hundred rivers boil; mountain peaks suddenly collapse.", "High banks become valleys; deep valleys become mounds.", "Alas for people today—why do they still not take warning?", "Huangfu is minister; Fan is minister of education; Jiabo is steward; Zhongyun is steward of meals; Zouzi is inner historian; Jue manages horses; Yu is master of the palace guard.", "The glamorous consort's arrogance is at its height; they all hold high office together.", "This Huangfu—can one say he does not keep to the seasons?", "Why assign me labor yet not come to consult with me?", "You tear down my walls and house; the fields all become weeds and filth.", "You even say I have not harmed you—that ritual and law are simply thus.", "Huangfu thinks himself very wise and builds a capital at Xiang.", "He chooses three officials to handle affairs—truly gathering much by taxation.", "He will not leave a single old minister to guard our king.", "He chooses those with carriages and horses and moves them to live at Xiang.", "I strive at my work and dare not speak of the hardship.", "Without guilt or fault, yet slander clamors loudly.", "The calamities of the people below do not fall from Heaven.", "Talk and laugh to your face, hate behind your back—all of it made by men.", "Far away, my hometown also makes me deeply ill.", "The four directions have surplus; I alone dwell in sorrow.", "Others are not without ease; I alone dare not rest.", "Heaven's mandate does not follow the usual way; I dare not learn from friends to seek ease for myself."], "xy-034": ["Vast blue Heaven does not long bestow its virtue.", "It sends down mourning, turmoil, and famine, cutting down the states of the four directions.", "Heaven's wrath is fierce; it does not consider or plan.", "It lets the guilty go free and covers over their crimes.", "As for these who are without guilt—they follow one another into suffering.", "The Zhou clan has already fallen; there is nowhere to settle and rest.", "Governing high officials scatter and live apart; none know my hardship.", "The three dukes and high officials will not serve diligently morning and evening.", "Lords of states and feudal princes will not attend the king day and night.", "We hoped they would turn toward good, but they go out and do evil instead.", "Alas, blue Heaven—upright words are not heeded.", "Like setting out on a long road yet having nowhere to arrive.", "Gentlemen all—each be careful of yourselves.", "Why do you not fear one another? Do you not fear Heaven?", "War has taken shape and does not withdraw; famine has taken shape and does not go well.", "I, a near attendant, grow haggard with sorrow day by day.", "Gentlemen all—you will not remonstrate or advise.", "Pleasant words you answer; when slander comes you withdraw.", "Alas that one cannot speak—it is not the tongue's fault, but that the self has suffered torment enough.", "Those who can speak get by well—clever words flow like water and place themselves in ease!", "As for holding office—it is both urgent and dangerous.", "Say one must not obey, and you offend the Son of Heaven; say one may obey, and you draw friends' resentment.", "I urge you to move to the royal capital.", "Yet you say you still have no household.", "Anxious thoughts weep blood; not a single word fails to draw resentment.", "When you left your dwelling before—who went with you to build a house?"], "xy-035": ["Heaven's wrath is fierce, covering the land below.", "Plans are crooked and not upright—when will they ever stop?", "Good counsel is not heeded; bad counsel is adopted instead.", "I look at these plans—they are also quite terrible.", "Echoing and slandering—also deeply sad.", "What is planned well is all contradicted.", "What is planned poorly is all followed.", "I look at these plans—where will they end up?", "My tortoise-shell divination is already weary; it no longer tells me fortune or misfortune.", "Counselors are too many, so nothing gets done.", "Speeches fill the court—who dares take responsibility?", "Like consulting passersby about the journey, so one does not find the right road.", "Alas for such planning—not taking the former people as the rule, not taking the great Way as the constant.", "Only listening to shallow words, only contending over shallow words.", "Like building a house on the great road and asking everyone—so it cannot be finished.", "Though the state is not very settled, there are the wise and also the unwise.", "Though the people are not very well-off, there are the clear-sighted and the good planners, the reverent and those who govern.", "Like a spring rushing forth—do not follow one another into shared ruin.", "Dare not wrestle a tiger barehanded; dare not cross a river on foot.", "People know only one thing and not the rest.", "Trembling with care, as if facing a deep abyss, as if treading thin ice."], "xy-036": ["The little turtledove spreads its wings and flies up to the high sky.", "My heart is sorrowful, thinking of the former people of the past.", "Dawn comes and still I cannot sleep, remembering both father and mother.", "The wise and sagely drink wine mildly and can restrain themselves.", "The ignorant and benighted, once drunk, think themselves rich enough.", "Each be careful of your bearing—Heaven's mandate will not come again.", "In the wilds there are beans and legumes; the common people go to gather them.", "The moth larva has young; the potter wasp carries them off to raise.", "Instruct your children; with the good way make them resemble it.", "Look at that wagtail, flying and calling as it goes.", "I hurry along day by day; you campaign far month by month.", "Rise early and sleep late; do not disgrace those who gave you birth.", "The jiao-jiao calling mulberry finch pecks millet along the garden plots.", "Alas for me, poor, sick, and alone—I fear I must face lawsuit and prison.", "Holding millet grains to divine—from where can a good omen come?", "The mild and careful person is like one perched on a high tree.", "Anxious and cautious, as if facing a deep valley.", "Trembling with care, as if treading thin ice."], "xy-037": ["That happy crow returns in flight with calm and ease.", "Everyone lives well—only I fall into hardship.", "What offense have I before Heaven?", "And what is my crime?", "The sorrow in my heart—what am I to do?", "The level great road now grows thick with weeds.", "My heart is sorrowful, aching as if pounded with a pestle.", "I doze fully clothed and sigh long; sorrow ages a person.", "The sorrow in my heart—pain like a headache.", "Mulberry and catalpa trees—one must treat them with reverence.", "Whom one looks up to is none but father; whom one relies on is none but mother.", "Am I not of the skin and fur?", "Am I not attached to the inner lining?", "Heaven gave me birth—where is my destiny?", "Those dense willows—cicadas call hui-hui; there is deep pool water, reeds thick and close.", "Like a boat following the current, not knowing where it goes; the heart is sorrowful, with no time even to doze.", "Deer run with slow, measured steps.", "Pheasants crow at dawn, still seeking their mates.", "Like a damaged tree, sick and without branches.", "The sorrow in my heart—does no one know it?", "Look at that rabbit caught in a net—still someone lets it go.", "A dead person on the road—still someone buries him.", "The gentleman's heart is so hard as this.", "The sorrow in my heart—tears have already fallen.", "The gentleman believes slander as if accepting urged wine.", "The gentleman shows no kindness and does not slowly inquire.", "To fell a tree one needs a rope to pull; to split firewood one follows the grain.", "Letting the truly guilty go free, yet laying the crime on me.", "There is no mountain that is not high; there is no spring that is not deep.", "Gentlemen, do not speak lightly—there are ears pressed to the wall listening.", "Do not go to my fish weir; do not touch my fish creel.", "I myself am still not tolerated—what spare thought have I for what comes after?"], "xy-038": ["Far blue Heaven—like father and mother.", "Without guilt or fault, yet the chaos is so great.", "Heaven is already fierce enough; I am sure of my innocence.", "Heaven is far too indulgent; I am sure I am without blame.", "When chaos first arose, slander was already tolerated.", "When chaos rose again, gentlemen believed the slander.", "If gentlemen would grow angry, the chaos might stop quickly.", "If gentlemen would employ the worthy, the chaos might cease quickly.", "Gentlemen repeatedly swear oaths, yet chaos grows instead.", "Gentlemen trust thieves, and chaos thus turns violent.", "The thieves' words are very sweet, and chaos thus intensifies.", "They are not reverent or faithful to their posts—they only add sickness to the king.", "The tall ancestral temple was built by gentlemen.", "Ordered great plans were set by sages.", "Whatever hearts others have, I can gauge them.", "The hopping crafty rabbit meets a dog and is caught.", "Supple fine wood—gentlemen plant it.", "Coming and going rumors—the heart counts them one by one.", "Exaggerated big talk comes out of the mouth.", "Clever words like organ reeds—thick-skinned indeed.", "What kind of person is that?", "Living by the riverside among the water plants.", "Without fist-strength or courage, making only the ladder of disorder.", "Legs ulcered and feet swollen—where is your courage?", "Schemes grow more and more—how many can your faction be?"], "xy-039": ["What kind of person is that?", "His scheming mind is deep and dangerous.", "Why pass my fish weir yet not enter my gate?", "Whom is he following?", "They say he follows Lord Bao.", "The two travel one road together—who caused this disaster?", "Why pass my fish weir yet not come in to comfort me?", "It was not like this before—now you say I am not worth keeping.", "What kind of person is that?", "Why pass by the road before my hall?", "I hear his voice but do not see his form.", "Before people he knows no shame; before Heaven he knows no fear.", "What kind of person is that?", "He is like a gust of swirling wind.", "Why not come from the north?", "Why not come from the south?", "Why pass my fish weir?", "Only to throw my heart into confusion.", "When you walk slowly, you have no time to pause.", "When you walk in haste, you somehow have time to oil the cart.", "Come once—how I long for it.", "If on return you enter the gate, my heart will ease.", "If you return yet do not enter, then it is hard to measure, hard to know.", "Come once—and put my heart at rest.", "Elder brother blows the xun; younger brother blows the chi.", "I and you are like beads on one string—yet I trust you do not understand me.", "Set out the three animals—pig, dog, and chicken—to curse you.", "If you were a ghost or a water demon, one could not catch you.", "Yet you have this face, and look at people without a standard.", "I make this fine song to pursue your fickleness to the end."], "xy-040": ["Patterns lush and brilliant—woven into this shell-brocade.", "Those who bring slander go much too far!", "Mouths open wide and broad—become that southern Winnowing Basket star.", "Those who bring slander—who plots with them?", "Whispering privately, coming and going lightly, plotting to harm people.", "Speak carefully—someone will say you cannot be trusted.", "Clever tongues like organ reeds, flipping back and forth, plotting to bring slander.", "Do they not accept your words?", "In the end disaster will turn upon you.", "The arrogant strut in triumph; the hardworking worry in agitation.", "Blue Heaven, blue Heaven—look upon those arrogant ones; pity these hardworking ones.", "Those who bring slander—who plots with them?", "Seize those slanderers and throw them to jackals and tigers.", "If jackals and tigers will not eat them, throw them to the northern wasteland.", "If the north will not take them, throw them to blue Heaven to deal with!", "The road to the willow garden lies close by Muqiu.", "The palace eunuch Mengzi composed this poem.", "Gentlemen all—please listen carefully."], "xy-041": ["The east wind blows xi-xi, bringing rain with it.", "In times of fear and dread, there was only you and me.", "When ease and joy were near, you cast me aside instead.", "The east wind blows xi-xi, bringing whirlwinds with it.", "In times of fear and dread, you held me in your arms.", "When ease and joy were near, you cast me off as if forgotten.", "The east wind blows xi-xi; mountains stand towering and high.", "There is no grass that does not die; there is no tree that does not wither.", "You forget my great kindness and remember only my small grievances."], "xy-042": ["That tall artemisia—it is not truly e but green artemisia.", "Alas, alas, my parents—how hard you labored to give me birth.", "That tall artemisia—it is not truly e but male artemisia.", "Alas, alas, my parents—how worn you were to give me birth.", "When the small bottle is empty, it is the shame of the great wine vessel.", "For the orphaned to live is worse than dying sooner.", "Without a father, what is there to rely on?", "Without a mother, what is there to lean on?", "Going out, I carry sorrow; coming in, it is as if I have no home to return to.", "Father gave me birth; mother nursed me.", "You stroked me and raised me, grew me and taught me, cared for me and watched over me again and again, holding me when going out and coming in.", "I wish to repay this kindness.", "Heaven's kindness has no end!", "The southern mountains stand lie-lie and steep; the swirling wind blows fa-fa and fierce.", "Everyone lives well—why am I alone the one who suffers!", "The southern mountains stand lü-lü and steep; the swirling wind blows fu-fu and fierce.", "Everyone lives well—I alone cannot support them to the end!"], "xy-043": ["The gui vessels are full of food; the jujube rice-spoons have long curved handles.", "The great road is level as a whetstone, straight as an arrow.", "Gentlemen walk upon it; lesser people watch from the side.", "Looking back once, tears flow freely.", "In the far and near places of the east, the looms stand empty.", "Twisted hemp sandals must yet tread frost and snow.", "Frivolous young lords walk upon that great road.", "Coming and going, they make my heart ache.", "There is a cold spring flowing aside—do not soak the already-cut firewood.", "Sleepless with sorrow, sighing long—alas for us hardworking people.", "This cut firewood can still be loaded and carted away.", "Alas for us hardworking people—we too might rest a while.", "Sons of easterners are assigned only to hard labor with no one to comfort them.", "Sons of westerners wear clothes bright and splendid.", "Sons of boatmen wear coats of bear and brown-bear fur.", "Sons of private household servants fill the posts of a hundred offices.", "Some drink wine; some cannot even get thin gruel.", "Some wear fine pendant gems; some lack even enough mixed pendants for length.", "In the sky there is the Milky Way, shining with light.", "Standing on tiptoe to watch that Weaver Girl star—seven times she moves in a day.", "Though she moves seven times, she cannot weave a complete bolt of cloth.", "The bright Oxherd star cannot pull a carriage box.", "In the east there is the Dawn Star; in the west there is Changgeng.", "The curved Heavenly Net star is arrayed across the sky.", "In the south there is the Winnowing Basket star, yet it cannot be used to winnow.", "In the north there is the Dipper star, yet it cannot be used to ladle wine.", "In the south there is the Winnowing Basket star, tongue drawn in as if to swallow.", "In the north there is the Dipper star, its western handle tilted high."], "xy-044": ["The fourth month is already summer; in the sixth month the heat grows fierce.", "Were the ancestors not people? Why harden their hearts to make me suffer?", "Autumn days are bleak and chill; a hundred plants all wither.", "Pain of chaos and exile—where shall I turn to go?", "Winter days are lie-lie cold; swirling winds blow fa-fa and fierce.", "Everyone lives well—why am I alone the one who suffers!", "On the mountains grow fine flowering trees—chestnuts and plums.", "Yet they are ruined by wreckers—I do not know whose fault!", "Look at that spring water—sometimes clear, sometimes muddy.", "I meet disaster day after day—how can one say I get by well?", "The rolling Jiang and Han are the guiding cords of the southern states.", "Worn out in office—is there truly no one who is close to me?", "I am not a quail or a kite, yet I wish to spread wings and fly to heaven.", "I am not a sturgeon or a tuna, yet I wish to dive and flee into the deep abyss.", "On the mountains grow ferns and wei greens; in the lowlands grow wolfberry and yi trees.", "The gentleman made this song only to tell of sorrow."], "xy-045": ["Climbing that northern mountain to gather wolfberries.", "A sturdy gentleman, busy with official duties morning and evening.", "The king's business never ends, making my parents worry for me.", "Under all heaven, nowhere is not the king's land; within the four seas, no one is not the king's subject.", "The high officials assign unevenly; I alone have especially heavy duties.", "Four horses run peng-peng; the king's business bustles in confusion.", "They praise me as not yet old and call me still strong.", "My strength is still vigorous, managing and rushing in all directions.", "Some rest in idle ease; some wear themselves out for the state; some lie stretched on beds; some run without stopping.", "Some know nothing of summons and orders; some labor in bleak hardship; some lounge and recline; some are entangled in the king's business.", "Some sink into drinking and pleasure; some fear in bleak dread of guilt; some go in and out making empty talk; some do nothing at all."], "xy-046": ["Do not push that great cart—you will only raise dust for yourself.", "Do not dwell on a hundred worries—you will only make yourself sick with pain.", "Do not push that great cart—dust darkens and covers the sky.", "Do not dwell on a hundred worries—you will not walk out into the light.", "Do not push that great cart—dust chokes and strikes the face.", "Do not dwell on a hundred worries—you will only increase your own burden."], "xy-047": ["Bright bright Heaven above shines down upon the land below.", "I set out west on campaign and reach the remote waste of Jiaoye.", "Setting out on an auspicious day in the second month, I have already passed through cold and heat.", "The sorrow in my heart is bitterly poisonous.", "Thinking of those careful, reverent people, tears fall like rain.", "Do I not long to go home?", "I fear this net of guilt!", "When I left long ago, sun and moon were just renewing the old with the new.", "When can I return?", "Another year is nearly at its end.", "Thinking of myself alone, yet my duties are especially many.", "The sorrow in my heart—hardship leaves me no leisure.", "Thinking of those careful, reverent people, I look back with lingering care!", "Do I not long to go home?", "I fear this rebuke and anger.", "When I left long ago, sun and moon were just in warmth.", "When can I return?", "Government affairs grow ever more pressing.", "Another year reaches its end—gathering mugwort, harvesting beans and legumes.", "The sorrow in my heart is sadness I brought upon myself.", "Thinking of those careful, reverent people, I rise, go out, and lodge away from home.", "Do I not long to go home?", "I fear this fickleness.", "Alas for you gentlemen—do not always seek a secure place.", "Reverently fulfill your posts; associate with the upright.", "When the spirits hear this, they will treat you with the good way.", "Alas for you gentlemen—do not always seek rest.", "Reverently fulfill your posts; love the way of uprightness.", "When the spirits hear this, they will grant you great blessings."], "xy-048": ["Strike the bells jiang-jiang; the Huai River flows vast—anxiety and aching grief.", "Good people and gentlemen—remember trustworthiness unforgotten.", "Strike the bells jie-jie; the Huai River flows jie-jie—anxiety and sorrow.", "Good people and gentlemen—their virtue is not crooked.", "Strike the bells and beat the great drums; the Huai has three islets—anxiety and unrest.", "Good people and gentlemen—their virtue does not deceive.", "Strike the bells qin-qin; play the se and the qin; sheng and stone chimes sound in harmony.", "Play the elegant music and the southern music; dance with the yue flute without losing the beat."], "xy-049": ["Tribulus grows thick in clusters—go cut away its thorns.", "Why was this done in former times?", "In order to plant millet and broomcorn millet.", "My millet grows yu-yu and lush; my broomcorn millet grows yi-yi and even.", "My granaries are already full; my open stores pile up by the hundred million.", "Use them to make wine and food, to offer in sacrifice; invite the impersonator of the dead to sit and urge the feast—pray for great blessings.", "In solemn ranks with dignified bearing, wash your cattle and sheep and go to the winter and autumn sacrifices.", "Some flay, some cook; some set out, some present.", "The invocator sacrifices at the temple gate; the rites are thoroughly clear and complete.", "The ancestors come into the hall; the spirit-guardian comes forward to partake.", "The filial grandson receives celebration; the reward is great blessings—boundless longevity!", "The kitchen staff step ji-ji and busy; the sacrificial meat on the stands is plentiful—some roasted, some grilled.", "The hostess is reverent and quiet; the dishes in the dou vessels are abundant.", "Acting as host and guest, pledging cups cross back and forth.", "The rites all fit the rules; laughter and talk all fit the occasion.", "The spirit-guardian has descended; the reward is great blessings—longevity comes in reply!", "I am thoroughly careful; the rites have no error.", "The working invocator delivers the announcement and goes to bestow favor on the filial grandson.", "Fragrant filial sacrifice—the spirits love this food and drink.", "They grant you a hundred blessings, as timed and as prescribed.", "Both orderly and swift; both upright and carefully restrained.", "Forever grant you utmost blessings—by the ten thousand, by the hundred million!", "The rites are complete; bells and drums stand ready; the filial grandson takes his place; the working invocator announces—the spirits are all drunk; the august impersonator rises.", "Strike the bells to send off the impersonator; the spirit-guardian returns.", "The stewards and the hostess clear away the offerings without delay.", "Uncles and brothers feast together in private.", "The instruments are all brought in and sounded, to enjoy at ease the blessings that come after.", "Your dishes have been served—no one complains; all congratulate.", "Drunk and full, old and young all bow their heads.", "The spirits love this food and drink and make the lord long-lived.", "Very smooth, very timely—carry the rites through to the end.", "Sons and grandsons—do not abolish them; keep them long in practice!"], "xy-050": ["That stretching southern mountain range was leveled by Yu the Great.", "Plains and lowlands are cleared and orderly; the great-grandson farms here.", "I mark boundaries and arrange the field acres, setting ridges north, south, east, and west.", "Heaven's dark clouds gather densely.", "Rain and snow fall fen-fen; fine drizzle mai-mu is added.", "Both generous and moistening; both soaking and sufficient.", "They grow my hundred grains.", "Field boundaries are orderly yi-yi; millet and broomcorn millet flourish yu-yu.", "The great-grandson's harvest is used to make wine and food.", "Offer them to the impersonator and the guests—longevity to ten thousand years.", "In the fields stand small huts; on the boundaries grow melons.", "Peel and pickle them into zu; offer them to the august ancestors.", "The great-grandson lives long and receives Heaven's blessings.", "Sacrifice with clear wine, followed by a red bull, offering to the ancestral fathers.", "Take up the luan-bell knife, part the sacrificial animal's hair, and take its blood and fat.", "The winter sacrifice is offered; fragrance spreads in all directions.", "The rites are thoroughly clear and complete.", "The ancestors come into the hall.", "They reward with great blessings.", "Boundless longevity."], "xy-051": ["That broad great field yields tens of thousands every year.", "I take out the old grain to feed my farmers.", "From ancient times there have been rich years.", "Now going to the southern acres—some weed, some heap earth around the roots.", "Millet and broomcorn millet grow ni-ni and lush; the elders rest among them and advance my outstanding young men.", "With my pure millet and broomcorn millet, and my sacrificial sheep, sacrifice to the god of the soil and to the four directions.", "My fields are already fine—this is the farmers' celebration.", "Qin, se, and drums welcome the Field Ancestor.", "Pray for sweet rain to help my broomcorn millet and millet, and to nurture my sons and daughters.", "The great-grandson has arrived, bringing his wife and children.", "Food is sent to the southern acres; the field officer sees it and rejoices.", "He draws those left and right near to taste whether the flavor is good.", "Grain seedlings fill the acres in good order—fine and abundant harvest.", "The great-grandson does not grow angry; the farmers can be diligent and alert.", "The great-grandson's crops pile high like thatch roofs, like cart beams.", "The great-grandson's grain stores are like small hills, like high platforms.", "Then seek a thousand granaries; then seek ten thousand cartloads.", "Millet, broomcorn millet, rice, and sorghum—this is the farmers' celebration.", "Reward with great blessings—boundless longevity."], "xy-052": ["In the great fields the crops are many; seeds are chosen, tools ready, all affairs in order.", "With my sharp plowshare I begin tilling the southern acres.", "Sowing a hundred grains, they grow upright and full; the great-grandson is well pleased.", "Already headed, already shelled; already firm and fine—no empty husks, no weeds.", "Clear away the stem borers and leaf-eaters, and also the root-gnawing pests—do not harm the tender shoots in my fields.", "The Field Ancestor has spiritual power—cast the pests into the blazing fire.", "Dark clouds rise qi-qi; rain falls qi-qi in abundance.", "Rain falls first on my public fields, then reaches my private fields.", "Over there, uncut tender grain; over here, unbound sheaves; over there, dropped sheaves; over here, leftover ears.", "All become benefits for the widows.", "The great-grandson has arrived, bringing his wife and children.", "Food is sent to the southern acres; the field officer sees it and rejoices.", "Coming to the burnt offerings of the four directions, with red oxen and black pigs, and with millet and broomcorn millet.", "Use them to offer in sacrifice and pray for great blessings."], "xy-053": ["Look at that Luo River—its waters are yang-yang, broad and wide.", "The gentleman has arrived; fortune and salary pile up like thatch.", "Kneepads of soft leather shine vermillion—used to command the six armies.", "Look at that Luo River—its waters are yang-yang, broad and wide.", "The gentleman has arrived; jade ornaments on his scabbard gleam.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years and keep his household.", "Look at that Luo River—its waters are yang-yang, broad and wide.", "The gentleman has arrived; fortune and salary all gather together.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years and keep his state and house."], "xy-054": ["Flowers bloom shang-shang in full glory; leaves grow xu-xu and lush.", "I meet that person; my heart opens in ease and joy.", "My heart opens in ease and joy—thus there is fair renown and a secure place.", "Flowers bloom shang-shang in full glory, a yellow stretch of yun-yun.", "I meet that person; he has his own patterned order and measure.", "He has his own patterned order and measure—thus there is celebration.", "Flowers bloom shang-shang in full glory, some yellow, some white.", "I meet that person, driving four black-and-white horses.", "Driving four black-and-white horses, the six reins gleam finely.", "Go left, go left—the gentleman is fitting in all.", "Go right, go right—the gentleman is fully equipped.", "Just because he is fully equipped, he can inherit ancestral virtue."], "xy-055": ["The jiao-jiao calling mulberry finch has patterned feathers.", "Happy is the gentleman—receiving Heaven's blessings.", "The jiao-jiao calling mulberry finch has patterned neck feathers.", "Happy is the gentleman—a screen for a myriad states.", "A screen and a ridgepole—the feudal lords take him as their measure.", "Without restraint and without careful caution, the blessings received are not many.", "The rhinoceros-horn cup curves; fine wine is thought soft and mild.", "In dealings with others, without arrogance—a myriad blessings come and gather."], "xy-056": ["Mandarin ducks fly, fly—catch them with nets and snares.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; fortune and salary suit him well.", "Mandarin ducks settle on the fish weir and fold the left wing.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years and fittingly enjoy lasting blessings.", "The riding horses are in the stable; chop fodder and feed to raise them.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; fortune and salary nurture him.", "The riding horses are in the stable; feed them and chop fodder to raise them.", "May the gentleman live ten thousand years; fortune and salary comfort him."], "xy-057": ["That lofty leather cap—what is it for, after all?", "Your wine is fine; your dishes are good.", "Are they outsiders?", "They are brothers, not others.", "Mistaken and dodder vines cling to pine and cypress.", "Before seeing the gentleman, anxiety runs yi-yi; once seeing the gentleman, one may almost rejoice.", "That lofty leather cap—when after all is it awaited?", "Your wine is fine; your dishes are timely.", "Are they outsiders?", "The brothers have all come.", "Mistaken and dodder vines cling to the pine.", "Before seeing the gentleman, anxiety runs bing-bing; once seeing the gentleman, one may almost gain benefit.", "That lofty leather cap sits upon the head.", "Your wine is fine; your dishes are abundant.", "Are they outsiders?", "They are brothers and nephews and maternal uncles.", "Like falling snow—what falls first is sleet.", "Death and mourning have no fixed time; days of meeting are few.", "Tonight drink and make merry; gentlemen, just feast."], "xy-058": ["The axle-pin clicks jian-guan—thinking of that fair young woman going to be married.", "It is not hunger, not thirst—it is fine virtue coming to meet.", "Though there are not many close friends?", "Still feast and rejoice.", "Against that level forest gather long-tailed pheasants.", "A beauty in her prime teaches with fine virtue.", "Feast and gain fair renown; love you and never tire.", "Though there is no fine wine?", "Still please drink a little.", "Though there are no fine dishes?", "Still please eat a little.", "Though there is no fine virtue to match?", "May you come and be of one heart with me.", "Climbing that high ridge to cut oak for firewood.", "Cutting oak for firewood—leaves grow xu-xu and lush.", "Rare to meet you; my heart opens in ease and joy.", "High mountains make one look up; great roads make one follow.", "Four stallions without rest; the six reins harmonious as qin strings.", "Meeting you in this new marriage comforts my heart."], "xy-059": ["Buzzing bluebottle flies settle on the fence.", "Harmonious, easygoing gentlemen—do not believe slander.", "Buzzing bluebottle flies settle on the thorns.", "Slanderers have no standard; they throw the states of the four directions into chaos.", "Buzzing bluebottle flies settle on the hazel trees.", "Slanderers have no standard; they drive a wedge between us two."], "xy-060": ["Guests first enter the banquet; left and right are in orderly ranks.", "Bian and dou vessels stand in neat rows; dishes and fruits are set out.", "The wine is mellow and sweet; drinking is thoroughly harmonious.", "Bells and drums are already set; raising cups to urge wine is done with ease.", "The great target is already raised; bows and arrows are already drawn.", "The archers have gathered; present your shooting merit.", "Hit that bull's-eye and pray to make you drink as forfeit.", "Yue-flute dance, sheng and drums—music played in harmony.", "Offer entertainment to the illustrious ancestors, to match the hundred rites.", "The hundred rites have all arrived—grand and numerous.", "Grant you great blessings; sons and grandsons all enjoy ease and joy.", "Ease and joy together; each presents his own talent.", "Guests seek their own partners; the host comes in again to accompany them.", "Fill that great cup and present what suits your timing.", "Guests first enter the banquet, mild and reverent.", "Before they are drunk, their bearing is solemn and careful fan-fan.", "Once drunk, their bearing turns frivolous and flipping.", "Leaving their seats and shifting about, they repeatedly rise to dance lightly xian-xian.", "Before they are drunk, their bearing is cautious and restrained yi-yi.", "Once drunk, their bearing loses composure bi-bi.", "This is what is called drunk—not knowing one's own place and order.", "Guests already drunk shout and make uproar.", "They disorder my bian and dou; repeatedly they rise to dance askew.", "This is what is called drunk—not knowing one's own faults.", "Leather caps worn crooked and tilted; repeatedly they dance suo-suo without stopping.", "If drunk they go out, everyone receives their blessing.", "If drunk they still will not go out—this is what is called ruined virtue.", "Drinking is fine, only so long as there is graceful bearing.", "Of all these who drink, some are drunk and some are not.", "A wine supervisor has already been set, or a scribe assists.", "Those who are drunk are not good; those who are not drunk feel shame instead.", "Do not indulge and obey; do not let great neglect arise.", "Do not say what should not be said; do not speak of what should not be followed.", "Following drunken talk into nonsense can force out a ram without horns.", "Three cups and already not clear-headed—how much more dare one drink further."], "xy-061": ["Fish swim among the algae; large heads are ban-ban and round.", "The king is in Hao, drinking in harmony and joy.", "Fish swim among the algae; long tails sway shen-shen.", "The king is in Hao, drinking in harmony and joy.", "Fish swim among the algae, leaning against the rushes.", "The king is in Hao, dwelling at ease with leisure."], "xy-062": ["Gathering and gathering soybeans—fill them in baskets large and small.", "The gentleman comes to court—what shall we grant him?", "Though one says there is nothing to grant?", "A great road carriage and the horses to drive it.", "And what else shall we grant him?", "A black dragon robe and an embroidered fu-patterned skirt.", "By the gushing threshold spring, go gather that celery.", "The gentleman comes to court—look at his banners.", "Banners flutter pi-pi; luan bells ring hui-hui.", "Driving three, driving four—the gentleman has arrived.", "Vermillion kneepads on the legs; slant-bound gaiters below.", "In dealings with others without neglect—this is what the Son of Heaven grants.", "Happy is the gentleman—the Son of Heaven appoints him.", "Happy is the gentleman—fortune and salary are added to him.", "Branches of the oak—leaves grow lush and full.", "Happy is the gentleman—he guards the Son of Heaven's states.", "Happy is the gentleman—a myriad blessings gather together.", "Those left and right are capable; all also follow in submission.", "A poplar boat drifts along; ropes are used to moor it.", "Happy is the gentleman—the Son of Heaven takes his measure.", "Happy is the gentleman—fortune and salary are richly granted him.", "At ease, at leisure—and so he comes to rest."], "xy-063": ["A well-tuned horn bow—when the string is loosened it springs the other way.", "Brothers and marriage kin—do not grow distant from one another.", "If you grow distant, the common people will all do likewise.", "If you instruct, the common people will all follow the model.", "Harmonious brothers have ample room to spare.", "Discordant brothers injure one another in turn.", "People of no goodness each resent the other from their own side.", "Receiving rank without yielding—when it comes to yourself, this means ruin.", "An old horse treated as a colt instead—without regard for the consequences.", "Like eating only to get full; like drinking only to take more.", "No need to teach a monkey to climb trees; like mud spread on mud, it naturally sticks.", "When gentlemen have fine and good plans, lesser people will then attach themselves.", "Rain and snow fall biao-biao; seeing the sun they melt away.", "Unwilling to treat people with humility—knowing only repeated arrogance.", "Rain and snow fall fu-fu; seeing the sun they become flowing water.", "Like southern Man, like eastern Yi—I therefore worry."], "xy-064": ["That lush willow tree—yet it is not fitting to rest beneath it.", "God on High shifts without constancy—do not go near of your own accord.", "I was sent to settle the state's affairs; afterward they banished me.", "That lush willow tree—yet it is not fitting to draw near.", "God on High shifts without constancy—do not bring sickness and disaster on yourself.", "I was sent to settle the state's affairs; afterward they drove me away.", "There are birds that fly high and can also touch Heaven.", "That person's heart—where does it mean to reach?", "Why have me settle the state's affairs, yet make me dwell in peril and suffer insult?"], "xy-065": ["Those people of the capital—fox furs shine yellow-yellow.", "Their bearing does not change from the usual; their speech has patterned order.", "Their conduct returns to the Zhou way—what a myriad people look up to.", "Those people of the capital wear sedge hats and black cloth caps.", "That noble lady—hair dense and straight as silk.", "I cannot see her—my heart is not glad.", "Those people of the capital—ear plugs filled with fine jade.", "That noble lady is called of the Yin and Ji houses.", "I cannot see her—my heart is knotted with gloom.", "Those people of the capital—sashes hang and flutter.", "That noble lady—curled hair lifted like a scorpion's tail.", "I cannot see her—I wish to follow her far away.", "It is not that one deliberately lets it hang—the sash simply has surplus.", "It is not that one deliberately curls it—the hair simply lifts upward.", "I cannot see her—how am I to hope and wait?"], "xy-066": ["All morning gathering lu grass—not enough to fill one handful.", "My hair is curled and tangled—go back and wash it.", "All morning gathering indigo—not enough to fill one lapel.", "We agreed on five days as the term; on the sixth he is still not seen.", "That man goes hunting; I store his bow for him.", "That man goes fishing; I arrange his fishing line for him.", "What does he catch?", "Bream and silver carp.", "Bream and silver carp—let us go and look."], "xy-067": ["Millet seedlings grow peng-peng and lush; cloudy rain moistens them.", "Far and long they travel south; Lord Shao comforts and rewards them.", "I carry on the shoulder, I push the handcart; I drive the carriage, I lead the ox.", "My task is already finished—time to speak of going home.", "I walk, I drive; I am of the host, I am of the troops.", "My task is already finished—time to speak of going home to settle.", "The solemn works at Xie—Lord Shao managed them.", "The fierce campaigning host—Lord Shao brought it to success.", "Plains and lowlands are already leveled; springs and streams already clear.", "Lord Shao has achievement; the king's heart is then at peace."], "xy-068": ["Mulberries in the lowland sway graceful; leaves grow nan-nan and lush.", "Seeing the gentleman—how great that joy is.", "Mulberries in the lowland sway graceful; leaves grow wo-wo and moist.", "Seeing the gentleman—how can one not be glad?", "Mulberries in the lowland sway graceful; leaves grow you-you deep green.", "Seeing the gentleman—his virtuous reputation is thoroughly firm.", "Loving in the heart—must it not be spoken aloud?", "Hidden in the heart—what day can it be forgotten!"], "xy-069": ["White blossoms made into jian grass; white thatch binds it.", "That person has grown distant, leaving me alone.", "Bright bright white clouds; dew moistens the jian and thatch.", "Fate is hard; that person will not help.", "The Biao pool flows north, soaking those rice fields.", "Whistling songs wound the heart, longing for that handsome one.", "Cutting mulberry branches for firewood, I bake them in the stove.", "Thinking of that handsome one truly wearies my heart.", "Bells struck in the palace—the sound carries outside.", "Thinking of you, my heart is restless cao-cao; you look at me with distant displeasure.", "There is a bald pelican at the fish weir; there is a white crane in the woods.", "Thinking of that handsome one truly wearies my heart.", "Mandarin ducks at the fish weir fold the left wing.", "That person is not good—fickle, without constant virtue.", "There is a flat stone; stepping on it feels lowly.", "That person has grown distant, leaving me sick with worry."], "xy-070": ["The mian-man calling yellow bird settles in the mountain bend.", "The road is so far—how hard I toil.", "Give him drink, give him food; instruct him, teach him.", "Order that rear carriage to take him aboard.", "The mian-man calling yellow bird settles in the mountain corner.", "Dare I fear the journey? I fear only falling behind.", "Give him drink, give him food.", "Instruct him, teach him.", "Order that rear carriage to take him aboard.", "The mian-man calling yellow bird settles on the mountainside.", "Dare I fear the journey? I fear only not arriving.", "Give him drink, give him food; instruct him, teach him.", "Order that rear carriage to take him aboard."], "xy-071": ["Fluttering gourd leaves—gather them and cook them.", "The gentleman has wine; pour and please taste.", "There is a rabbit—roasted and then baked.", "The gentleman has wine; pour and present to the guest.", "There is a rabbit—baked and then grilled.", "The gentleman has wine; pour and invite a return toast.", "There is a rabbit—baked and then roasted.", "The gentleman has wine; pour and repay one another."], "xy-072": ["Steep jagged rocks—how high they are.", "Mountains and rivers stretch far—how hard the toil.", "Warriors campaign eastward; there is no time to attend court.", "Steep jagged rocks—how perilously sheer.", "Mountains and rivers stretch far—when will they reach an end?", "Warriors campaign eastward; there is no time to show one's face.", "There are pigs with white trotters, crossing the waves in herds.", "The moon draws near the Net star, bringing torrential rain.", "Warriors campaign eastward; there is no time to attend to anything else."], "xy-073": ["The blossoms of the tiao vine have turned yellow yun-yun.", "The sorrow in my heart—how sad it is!", "The blossoms of the tiao vine—the leaves are still green.", "Had I known I would be like this, better never to have been born!", "A ewe with a large head and lean body; the Shen stars shine on an empty fish creel.", "People can eat a little—few can eat their fill!"], "xy-074": ["What grass does not turn yellow?", "What day is there without rushing about?", "What person is not pressed into service?", "Managing and rushing in all directions.", "What grass does not turn black?", "What person is not lonely and pitiful?", "Alas for us campaigners—alone treated as less than human.", "Not rhinoceroses, not tigers, yet we rush about in the open wilds.", "Alas for us campaigners—morning and evening without leisure.", "There are bushy foxes, coming and going in the deep grass.", "There are tall plank carts traveling on the great road."]};
